window.AKK_TYRANT_FATHER_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_TYRANT_FATHER_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: People from the imperial court Here to grab money","paragraphs":["“Clack, clack, clack.”","The crisp collision of the beads on the solid-gold abacus echoed through the spacious underground hall.","To Su Yaoyao’s ears, the sound was more beautiful than celestial music.","Dozens of rosewood chests stood open in the center of the hall.","Silver ingots gleamed white, gold sycees shone brilliantly, and stacks of banknotes were piled as high as little mountains.","This was the headquarters of the largest underground black market in the capital of the Great Yuan Kingdom.","Su Yaoyao lounged comfortably in a grand chair draped with an entire white tiger hide.","She crossed her legs without a shred of decorum, tapping her toe as it bobbed in the air.","In her left hand was a handful of sunflower seeds. With her right, she toyed with a golden abacus, humming a cheerful tune whose words were impossible to make out.","“Three prosperous connected shops in the eastern part of the city, valued at twenty-five thousand taels of silver.”","“The deed to the underground gambling den in the south of the city, valued at forty thousand taels.”","“And these several chests of ready cash just hauled out of the underground bank’s vault—one hundred and twenty thousand taels in all!”","The more Su Yaoyao counted, the more energized she became. Her beautiful, seductive eyes practically glowed green with greed.","Just an hour earlier, she had led this gang of black-market desperados in completely looting the capital’s number-one underground bank.","The banker who had dared to compete with her for business was currently hanging naked from a crooked tree outside the city, left to shiver in the cold wind.","“Boss is mighty! Boss is magnificent!”","Beside her, a burly man with a face full of flesh and a scar running straight across his left eye held out a bowl of tea with a deferential smile.","“Ever since you took over our black market, business has grown bigger and bigger. Following you, Boss, the brothers are finally getting a taste of the good life!”","Su Yaoyao spat out a sunflower-seed shell, took the tea bowl, and moistened her throat.","“This is nothing. Follow your boss, and I guarantee you’ll be eating well and drinking fine liquor every day from now on.”","Su Yaoyao had been a max-level poison doctor and mechanical engineer in the interstellar era. After transmigrating to ancient times, if she didn’t establish a monopoly and make a fortune, she would be letting down all the technology and ruthless ingenuity packed inside her head.","In this lawless underground world, morality was the bottom line.","And she had no bottom line.","Not only would she monopolize the capital’s black market, she would open branches throughout the entire kingdom.","Making money this quickly was far easier than working for a living in the interstellar era.","“Go. Add those several century-old wild ginseng roots in the storeroom to the accounts. Tomorrow, take them to the auction house and turn them into cash.”","Su Yaoyao waved her hand grandly, carrying herself like a general directing the fate of the world.","Scarface was just about to accept the order when a sudden change occurred.","“Boom!”","A deafening explosion rang out like thunder striking the ground.","The underground hall began to shake violently, and dust sifted down from the ceiling.","Quick as a flash, Su Yaoyao snatched the golden abacus off the table and stuffed it into her robes.","“What’s going on? An earthquake? Or did that banker come back from the dead with a bunch of ghosts to collect his debt?”","She frowned and unhappily brushed the dust from her clothes.","Bang!","Before anyone could react, the black market’s iron gate—said to be strong enough to withstand even an elephant—was blasted apart from the outside, shattered into countless splinters of wood and shards of metal.","The sharp fragments shot into the hall like a torrential downpour. Several black-market enforcers who failed to dodge in time were pierced like pincushions and collapsed into pools of blood, screaming.","The hall descended into chaos.","“Grab your weapons! Someone’s here to wreck the place!”","Scarface roared as he drew the nine-ring saber from his waist, his layers of flesh trembling.","The black-market enforcers had spent years living by the blade and reacted with astonishing speed. One after another, they drew their weapons and stared fixedly at the billowing smoke where the gate had been blown apart.","“Boss! This is bad! This is really bad!”","A blood-covered underling crawled out of the smoke, rolling and scrambling on all fours.","Crying out as he came, he left a long smear of blood across the floor while clawing his way toward Su Yaoyao.","“What are you wailing about? Even if the sky falls, someone taller will hold it up!”","Su Yaoyao remained firmly seated in her grand chair, without even uncrossing her legs.","“It’s not the sky falling... It’s—it’s the imperial army!”","The underling’s face was filled with terror as he desperately clutched at Scarface’s trouser leg.","“The Imperial Guards have broken in! The brothers outside are all dead!”","At those words, the entire hall fell silent.","Even Scarface, a hardened killer who had never batted an eye at taking a life, sucked in a sharp breath.","The Imperial Guards?","They were the royal troops who answered only to the emperor himself!","Though their black market was brazen, they had only ever dared to throw their weight around in the underground world.","The imperial court had always turned a blind eye to them. As long as they did not rebel, the two sides kept out of each other’s way.","What was happening today?","Had the authorities decided to raid the black market?","Su Yaoyao’s fingers stopped moving as she cracked sunflower seeds.","She didn’t care about the Imperial Guards.","What she cared about was the dozens of chests of gold and silver she had just seized.","“People from the imperial court? They’ve come to steal our money?”","Her eyes narrowed, and her expression gradually turned dangerous.","Step. Step. Step.","The steady, heavy rhythm of marching footsteps emerged from the smoke at the entrance.","The scrape and clank of heavy armor sounded with every step, each one pounding against the hearts of everyone present.","Along with those footsteps came a suffocating, terrifying killing intent.","It was so dense that it extinguished every trace of resistance in the black-market enforcers, as if icy water had been poured over them.","The temperature in the air plummeted. Even breathing became difficult.","The smoke slowly cleared.","A tall, slender figure stepped over the scattered limbs and severed bodies covering the floor and entered the underground hall.","The newcomer wore a dark black-and-gold dragon robe. Five-clawed golden dragons embroidered along the hem seemed to bare their teeth and brandish their claws in the firelight, so lifelike they appeared ready to leap from the fabric.","He was extraordinarily handsome, with deep, sharply defined features that looked as though they had been carved by knife and axe.","Yet his narrow eyes held a cruel, chilling savagery.","He looked like a bloodthirsty lone wolf that had just awakened and was preparing to slaughter everything in sight.","He was the master of the Great Yuan Kingdom, the reigning tyrant—Su Zhen.","In his hand, he carried a three-foot-long sword pointed downward, its blade gleaming coldly.","The legendary peerless sword.","The Dragon Spring Sword.","The imperial blade, symbolizing royal authority, dripped with glaring red blood.","“Drip... drip...”","Thick blood slid down the edge of the sword and struck the ground, splashing into clusters of scarlet plum blossoms.","In the dead-silent hall, the sound rang out like a death knell.","Behind Su Zhen surged several hundred fully armed Imperial Guards.","They held icy spears and surrounded the entire underground hall so completely that not even a fly could escape.","Their frigid killing intent sealed off every possible route of retreat.","Clang!","The nine-ring saber fell from Scarface’s hand.","His knees gave way, and he crashed heavily to the ground, his entire body shaking like a sieve.","“T-The emperor...”","It wasn’t only Scarface. The moment the black-market underlings recognized the dragon robe, their psychological defenses collapsed.","Every one of them threw down their weapons and knelt on the floor. Some were so terrified that they wet themselves on the spot, filling the air with a foul stench.","That was Su Zhen!","The most bloodthirsty tyrant in the history of the Great Yuan Kingdom!","Rumor had it that on the day he ascended the throne, he had all the families of the officials who opposed him—several hundred people in total—beheaded outside the Hall of Supreme Harmony. Blood had flowed like a river.","Anyone who caught his attention had to queue up to report to the King of Hell—and then cut in line.","“It’s over... It’s all over. We’re all going to be executed along with our entire families today...”","The underlings shut their eyes in despair, praying only that the tyrant would grant them a quick death.","Su Zhen came to a halt. His cold gaze swept across the hall like a radar.","At last, his eyes passed over everyone kneeling on the floor and landed directly on the center of the hall.","It landed on the only little girl who had neither knelt nor moved from the grand chair, where she sat with her legs crossed.","A bloodthirsty glint flashed in Su Zhen’s eyes.","He tightened his grip on the Longquan sword and strode toward Su Yaoyao, his long legs carrying him forward one step at a time.","The bloodstained tip of the sword scraped across the floor with an ear-piercing shriek.","Murderous intent descended upon Su Yaoyao like a tidal wave.","Su Zhen stopped in front of the grand chair and raised his arm.","The icy Longquan sword came to rest against Su Yaoyao’s slender, fair neck.","With the slightest exertion of his wrist, her perfectly good head would roll across the floor.","Life and death hung by a thread.","Yet even when faced with a predicament terrifying enough to shake an ordinary person to the core, Su Yaoyao did not so much as blink.","Her gaze did not linger on the tyrant or his bloodthirsty sword.","Instead, she looked past Su Zhen’s shoulder and fixed her eyes on the Imperial Guards behind him.","More precisely, she was staring at the heavy, finely crafted standard armor they wore.","Su Yaoyao’s eyes grew brighter and brighter as the calculations in her mind began to clatter away.","Wow, they’re all top-grade cold-iron linked armor!","The quality, the craftsmanship—what superb smelting materials!","If all five hundred-plus suits of heavy armor were stripped off and tossed into the furnace at the arms factory to be reforged...","Just how many muskets could they make? And how many glittering gold ingots could those be traded for?"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Is This My Mercurial Tyrant Dad","paragraphs":["The icy blade of a Longquan sword pressed against Su Yaoyao’s fair, slender neck.","In the dim firelight of the underground hall, the sharp blade reflected a bone-chilling gleam.","The thick, still-wet blood clinging to its edge trickled down her delicate skin, a shocking sight to behold.","All it would take was another half inch.","That petite head would come tumbling to the floor.","It was an utterly hopeless fight between life and death.","Standing above her, Su Zhen looked down at the young woman with cold, bloodthirsty eyes, as though she were nothing more than a lifeless object.","As the ruler of the Dayuan Empire—an emperor whose ruthless decisiveness in war had made the entire world tremble—he had witnessed countless people struggling on the brink of death.","Those ministers who preached benevolence and morality in court every day, proudly presenting themselves as men of lofty integrity, would still wet themselves in terror, sob uncontrollably, and kowtow for mercy when a butcher’s knife was truly placed against their throats.","What hope was there for some rough black-market thug, no better than a sewer rat?","And yet Su Zhen’s brows drew together slightly.","Something seemed... off.","Very off.","The seemingly weak and helpless young woman before him was facing a blade close enough to take her life at any moment.","But not even her eyelashes trembled.","She remained firmly seated in the grand chair draped with an entire white tiger pelt.","Even her boldly crossed leg showed no sign of lowering!","Su Zhen was an emperor who had clawed his way out of mountains of corpses and seas of blood. He was extraordinarily sensitive to killing intent and fear.","Yet in the young woman’s clear, luminous peach-shaped eyes, he could not find the slightest trace of panic or dread.","On the contrary, her eyes were frighteningly bright.","He had seen that look only in one creature before.","A prairie wolf that had gone three days and three nights without food, suddenly laying eyes on a plump, juicy piece of meat.","And now, the mighty Tyrant of Dayuan seemed to be that succulent piece of meat in this girl’s eyes.","Absurd!","Su Yaoyao’s gaze indeed did not linger for long on Su Zhen’s handsome, icy face.","She had merely taken a brief moment to admire those breathtaking features, as though they had been carved by knives and axes.","Then her attention was drawn to his clothes.","Good heavens! This was a dragon robe embroidered by hand with pure gold thread!","The black fabric shimmered faintly beneath the torchlight.","It was clearly made of the legendary finest silkworm silk—impervious to blades and spears, untouched by fire or water.","Then there was the swimming-dragon jade pendant hanging from his waist.","It was carved from an entire piece of mutton-fat white jade, smooth and warm, without a single impurity.","And the purple-gold crown securing his hair was set with a flawless pearl the size of a pigeon’s egg!","She was rich!","She was really, truly rich!","Su Yaoyao swallowed greedily in her mind, while the beads of an abacus clattered furiously in her head.","If she could find an opportunity to strip all of those treasures off him, she would have more than enough to build a few Gatling guns.","She could even open a small military-industrial factory with ease!","A transmigrator from the interstellar age, she was a max-level poison doctor and mechanic.","She had been poor for far too long. Now, all she saw in her eyes were precious metals and jewels that could be converted into industrial materials and funds for weapons.","Just as Su Yaoyao’s eyes lit up and she was frantically plotting how to rob the robber and pull off the biggest score of her life, a sharp, grating voice—like fingernails scraping across a blackboard—shattered the silence in the hall.","“How dare you, you brazen criminal! You’re on the verge of death, yet you still dare to look directly at His Majesty’s holy countenance? That is treasonous!”","A eunuch wearing a tall hat and sporting a smooth, hairless face hurried forward from behind the hundreds of fully armed Imperial Guards, waving a horsetail whisk threaded with gold.","His name was Li Fu, the chief eunuch of the Dayuan imperial palace and a trusted favorite at the emperor’s side.","But very few people knew that he was, in fact, the deepest mole that the powerful court minister and great general Lin Zhenxiong had planted beside the emperor.","Li Fu’s forehead was covered in sweat, and unmistakable anxiety and panic showed in his eyes.","Every so often, he had been looking up through the ventilation shaft of the underground hall to check the sky outside, his heart as frantic as an ant on a hot pan.","Tonight was the night his master had spent three whole years preparing for—the night of the final strike!","The bowl of calming soup laced with the Western Regions’ most potent poison, the Soul-Severing Draught, was already being kept warm in a purple-clay brazier in the imperial kitchen.","All they had to do was wait for the emperor to return to the palace and drink it.","The poison would take effect immediately, twisting his intestines with agony before making him bleed from all seven orifices and die. Not even the gods could save him.","Once that happened, his master’s grand ambition would be achieved without a hitch!","Yet at this most critical juncture, the emperor had suddenly taken leave of his senses.","He had insisted on personally gathering troops and leaving the palace to wipe out this underground black market.","If this delayed them and caused them to miss the ideal moment to administer the poison, ruining his master’s carefully laid plans, then even ten heads would not be enough to satisfy his master’s wrath.","They had to finish this quickly and persuade the emperor to return to the palace at once!","With that thought, Li Fu steeled himself and stepped forward. Pointing at Su Yaoyao, who sat as steady as Mount Tai in the grand chair, he began fanning the flames with reckless abandon.","“Your Majesty, just look at this woman! She has shifty eyes and a wretched appearance. She clearly isn’t a good person!”","“Before Your Majesty’s mighty dragon aura, she remains seated instead of kneeling. She is openly scorning imperial authority. Her crime is unforgivable!”","As he maliciously shouted, he anxiously urged Su Zhen on.","“Someone as filthy as this sewer rat is unworthy of sullying Your Majesty’s eyes.”","“Please issue the order, Your Majesty. Have her executed on the spot, and then we can return to the palace and let you rest as soon as possible!”","“If we delay any longer and Your Majesty’s calming soup grows cold, even a thousand deaths would not be enough to atone for this servant’s crime!”","Li Fu’s words sounded lofty and righteous.","Seated in the chair, Su Yaoyao could not help rolling her eyes dramatically.","This damned eunuch was so noisy.","Not only was his voice grating enough to raise goosebumps, but his eager, servile eagerness to see someone dead was even more nauseating.","Did he really think that she, a max-level poison doctor from the interstellar age, could be frightened so easily?","A mere ancient cold weapon could not even break through her protective force field.","If she had not been waiting to haul away all the gold, silver, and jewels filling the room, she would have tossed out a high-explosive smoke bomb long ago and escaped in the confusion.","Su Zhen turned his head and cast Li Fu a cold glance.","That single look seemed to be infused with shards of ice that had frozen for ten thousand years.","Li Fu’s legs went weak. He shut his mouth and dropped heavily to his knees.","“This servant spoke out of turn! This servant deserves death! Please spare me, Your Majesty!”","Although Su Zhen found Li Fu’s voice irritating, he also felt that this tiresome farce had gone on long enough.","She was nothing more than a black-market leader who did not know when to stop. Killing her was no great loss. The Dayuan Empire would hardly miss one life.","His wrist sank slightly, and killing intent surged in his deep eyes.","The blade of the Longquan sword pressed downward.","Its cold, razor-sharp edge cut through the tender skin of Su Yaoyao’s neck.","A faint sting reached her.","Bright-red beads of blood welled up, like red plum blossoms blooming across a field of snow.","The sudden pain finally pulled Su Yaoyao’s greedy attention away from the dragon robe.","Frowning, she looked at the man before her, whose entire body radiated a murderous aura and who killed without batting an eye.","He had a handsome face, but why did he start drawing blood at the slightest disagreement?","What a violent brute. He clearly had no understanding of maintaining a proper doctor-patient relationship!","Su Zhen’s gaze remained unmoved, as though he were looking at a corpse.","He was just about to exert force and bring this absurd night to an end.","But at that very moment, with life and death hanging by a thread—","a clear, melodious female voice rang out, carrying a hint of excited teasing.","It was like a thunderclap exploding across a flat plain, roaring through his mind!","Su Zhen’s movements came to an abrupt halt.","He glanced around.","The imperial guards surrounding him stood with their long halberds in hand, quiet as cicadas in winter, not daring to make a sound.","The chief eunuch, Li Fu, was still kneeling on the ground, trembling all over.","Then where had that crystal-clear voice come from?","Just as he was filled with doubt and beginning to wonder whether he had imagined it, the voice rang out again.","It echoed thunderously inside his head!","【So this is my moody, unpredictable Tyrant Dad? He’s pretty handsome!】","Su Zhen’s eyes widened as he stared in disbelief at the little girl beneath his sword, whose lips had not moved at all.","The Tyrant?","Dad?!","The girl’s lips were clearly sealed shut. So why was her voice drilling into his mind?!","Could sorcery truly exist in this world? Or had he been possessed by some evil spirit?","But that absurd voice showed no sign of stopping.","【What a shame. With such a handsome face, it’s going to turn purplish-black tonight.】","【He’s going to be poisoned to death on the dragon bed by that damned chief eunuch beside him, using Qianji poison. How tragic.】","Su Zhen’s pupils shook as if struck by a magnitude-ten earthquake!","Qianji poison?!","Poisoned to death?!","He turned his head and fixed his gaze on Li Fu, who was kneeling nearby, his face slick with sweat.","Li Fu flinched at the terrifying look the emperor suddenly cast his way.","He lowered his head guiltily, cold sweat soaking through his heavy eunuch’s robes.","Why did he feel as though His Majesty were looking at him like a corpse that would soon begin to rot?","A tempest raged through Su Zhen’s heart, and his breathing stopped for a moment.","Qianji poison was an ultimate poison from the Western Regions. It was colorless and odorless, and even the chief physician of the Imperial Medical Academy would have great difficulty detecting it.","This was a closely guarded imperial secret. How could this girl possibly know about it?","Who exactly was she?!","Before Su Zhen could recover from the earth-shattering information, the crisp female voice in his mind immediately tossed out an even more hair-raising thought.","【Well, it wouldn’t matter much if the Tyrant Dad died, but what a waste of those clothes.】","【If I stripped off that dragon robe while it’s still warm, and added the Eastern Pearl on his head, I could probably sell the whole lot for at least a hundred thousand taels, right?】","Su Zhen’s hand trembled around the Longquan sword."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: Oh, My Daughter—","paragraphs":["As an emperor who had clawed his way to the throne over mountains of corpses and seas of blood, Su Zhen had never experienced anything in his life that could be called trembling hands.","Yet now, the peerless Longquan sword that could slice through iron was quivering against Su Yaoyao’s neck.","His entire worldview was undergoing a devastating assault!","Su Zhen stared at the young girl before him.","Beneath the firelight, her lips had not moved.","Then where had that voice come from?!","【Hey, hey, hey! Hold it steady, old man! Don’t let your hands shake and sever my carotid artery!】","【There aren’t even tetanus shots in this ancient era, and your lousy sword is crawling with bacteria, okay?!】","【If you weren’t my Tyrant Dad—the father I’ve never even met—I would’ve blasted you with a handful of interstellar poison dust by now!】","That crisp feminine voice, carrying three parts nonchalance and seven parts disdain, exploded once more deep inside Su Zhen’s mind!","Su Zhen took a deep breath. His heart was pounding so hard it seemed ready to burst out of his chest.","Confirmed.","That voice really was coming from the girl’s heart!","Tyrant Dad?","Poisoned to death by the chief eunuch?","Strip off his imperial robe and sell it for a hundred thousand taels?","Su Zhen rapidly digested the explosive information.","He carefully examined Su Yaoyao’s clear, bright, peach-shaped eyes.","This face, these features—they resembled those of his deceased wife, who had died violently eight years ago, by at least seventy percent!","But this was no time to acknowledge a long-lost daughter.","Compared with the sudden appearance of a daughter, the Qianji poison threatening his life tonight was the blade hanging over his head.","It was a rare and deadly poison from the Western Regions. Even the chief physician of the Imperial Medical Bureau was helpless against it. How could this girl know every detail so clearly?","Su Zhen did not immediately withdraw the sword from Su Yaoyao’s neck.","He had to personally verify whether this voice was telling the truth.","The underground hall fell into deathly silence. Everyone held their breath.","Su Zhen turned his head.","His cold gaze, sharp as two blades of ice, fell upon the chief eunuch kneeling beside him, Li Fu.","Li Fu knelt on the floor, his forehead slick with sweat.","When he suddenly felt a suffocating killing intent envelop him, he shuddered.","“Y-Your Majesty?” Li Fu forced out a fawning smile.","Looking down at him from on high, Su Zhen’s lips curled into a smile that was not quite a smile.","“Li Fu.”","He drew out the name, his calm voice sending chills down the spine.","“This servant is here!” Li Fu’s entire body trembled as he lowered his head even further.","“You just said you were in such a hurry to urge Me back to the palace to rest?”","Su Zhen toyed with the hilt of his sword, his tone low and eerie. “Is My calming tonic ready?”","At the words “calming tonic,” Li Fu’s body visibly stiffened for half a second.","Though it lasted only a brief moment, it could never escape the eyes of a supreme expert like Su Zhen.","Li Fu swallowed and forced himself to remain composed as he raised his head.","“To answer Your Majesty, the tonic... the tonic has been kept warm in the purple clay stove in the imperial kitchen.”","“The heat is just right. It has been waiting for Your Majesty to return and enjoy it, so that it may ensure Your Majesty’s health and grant You a peaceful night’s sleep.”","A peaceful night’s sleep? More like eternal sleep!","Su Zhen’s gaze turned utterly cold.","He clearly caught the evasiveness deep in Li Fu’s eyes, saw the cold sweat involuntarily beading on his temples,","and noticed the unnatural twitch in the muscles of his left cheek when he answered.","His microexpressions had completely exposed the old dog’s murderous intentions!","Everything the girl had said in her heart was true!","This treacherous dog of a servant had truly colluded with outsiders and planned to poison him to death tonight!","【Wow, this old eunuch has terrible nerves. He’s already sweating bullets.】","【When he was talking, his eyes drifted down and to the right. That’s a classic lying microexpression.】","【What a shame for my Tyrant Dad. A mighty emperor of his generation, and he’s about to be sent off by a bowl of soup.】","Su Yaoyao was thoroughly enjoying the spectacle and continued to complain wildly in her heart.","She even clicked her tongue regretfully.","Listening to the girl’s gleeful remarks, Su Zhen’s chest heaved violently.","He did not know whether he should be angry at the treacherous servant’s treason, or at this unfilial daughter for hoping he would die so she could strip him of his clothes and sell them.","Suddenly, he moved.","“Heh.”","Su Zhen let out a low chuckle.","The laughter grew louder and louder, eventually becoming an unrestrained, booming roar that echoed through the hall.","“Hahahaha! Good! What a wonderful ‘peaceful night’s sleep’!”","His savage laughter reverberated through the underground hall, rattling everyone’s eardrums.","The Imperial Guards tightened their grips on their spears, while the black-market thugs were so terrified that they flattened themselves against the ground and frantically kowtowed.","Everyone thought the Tyrant had gone mad again and was about to begin another massacre.","Li Fu’s scalp went numb as he was consumed by an ominous premonition of death.","“Your Majesty... you...”","The laughter abruptly stopped.","Su Zhen’s gaze transformed into the very embodiment of a demon from hell.","Without wasting even half a word, he twisted his wrist, gripping the Longquan sword as he swung it backward.","The blade slashed toward Li Fu, who was kneeling on the ground!","Everyone saw only a blinding flash of silver cold light explode before their eyes.","“Splurt!”","The dull, horrifying sound of a blade slicing through flesh and bone rang out.","Li Fu’s expression froze on his face.","His mouth hung slightly open. He did not even have time to scream.","A thin red line appeared between his brows and extended all the way down to his groin.","“Crack.”","Li Fu’s body split apart like a watermelon sliced down the middle.","The two halves fell away from each other as he was cleaved cleanly in two!","Foul blood mixed with organs and sprayed everywhere, splattering the entire floor.","The chief eunuch of Great Yuan, a man of tremendous power, had been sent straight to the afterlife!","Silence.","The entire underground hall once again sank into suffocating silence.","A thick wave of blood and gore swept through the underground headquarters like a storm.","Several black-market thugs with weak stomachs felt their insides churn. They dropped to their knees and began vomiting violently.","Even the battle-hardened commander of the Imperial Guards sucked in a sharp breath, feeling somewhat tense.","To cleave his most trusted eunuch in half at the slightest provocation—the man’s methods were simply too brutal!","Su Yaoyao was stunned as well.","【Holy crap! His combat power is insane!】","【Clean and decisive. No pointless speeches—he just gets the job done. I like it!】","Hearing her thoughts, the corners of Su Zhen’s lips involuntarily lifted.","He stood in the pool of blood, yet not a single drop had touched his dark imperial robes. His presence was overwhelmingly domineering.","His deep gaze returned to Su Yaoyao.","Then he did something that shattered the worldview of everyone present.","Clang!","Su Zhen casually flung away the peerless divine weapon, the Longquan sword still drenched in blood, tossing it to the ground as if it were garbage.","Su Yaoyao’s eyes widened when she saw the precious sword land in the bloody water.","【What a waste! That’s the Longquan sword forged from meteoric iron from beyond the heavens!】","【There’s even a flawless emerald set into the hilt! And he just threw it away? That sword is worth at least fifty thousand taels!】","Just as Su Yaoyao’s heart ached over the money,","this cold-blooded Tyrant, this eternal emperor who slaughtered with ruthless decisiveness,","bent his knees.","On the bloodstained floor, he performed an impossibly smooth sliding kneel.","Then he threw himself at the foot of Su Yaoyao’s white-tiger-pelt armchair!","Under the horrified gazes of every Imperial Guard and black-market thug present—so horrified their eyeballs nearly fell from their sockets—","the Tyrant Su Zhen wrapped both arms around Su Yaoyao’s leg.","He raised his head, opened his mouth, and let out a mournful yet thunderous howl:","“My daughter—!”"]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Her Highness the Crown Princess, a Thousand Years, a Thousand Years, a Thousand Thousand Years","paragraphs":["“Girl—!”","The earth-shaking howl pierced through the thick stone walls of the underground hall, overpowering even the pungent stench of blood pooling across the floor.","The fully armed Imperial Guards, bristling with murderous intent, all stood frozen like tree trunks struck by lightning.","Their eyes were wide as they stared at their own Tyrant—the man who had just cleaved the chief eunuch in two without so much as blinking.","And now, this same Tyrant was kneeling in the bloodstained filth without a shred of dignity, clutching the thigh of the black-market boss!","The black-market underlings were scared out of their wits. They thought the Tyrant had suddenly gone mad.","“Those eyes, that nose, those lips...”","Su Zhen paid no attention to the way everyone around him was falling apart.","He tilted his head back, his eyes red-rimmed, tears pouring down his face like a burst dam.","He tugged up the sleeve of his dark-gold dragon robe—woven from silkworm silk worth a hundred thousand taels—and carelessly wiped the snot and tears from his face.","“She looks so much like you! Exactly like you!”","Su Zhen was so agitated that he could barely form a coherent sentence. His trembling finger pointed at Su Yaoyao’s face.","Su Yaoyao’s leg had gone numb from his embrace, and the corner of her mouth twitched violently.","She really couldn’t help herself. Right in front of this legendary Tyrant, she rolled her eyes so dramatically that it could have been considered an art form.","Who would have thought that this would only make Su Zhen cry even harder? He looked like a two-hundred-pound child who had been terribly wronged.","“Even the way you roll your eyes is exactly like your late mother!”","Su Zhen wailed. “It’s been eight years! I’ve been searching for you for eight whole years!”","“Back then, your mother died under mysterious circumstances, and you disappeared along with her as a newborn. I thought I’d never see you again in this lifetime!”","“Heaven has eyes! Heaven has eyes!”","Su Yaoyao sat stiffly in the white tiger-skin armchair, looking down at the Tyrant who was crying so hard his nose was running.","Inside, she was screaming like mad.","[No way! He recognizes me just like that?]","[Are ancient people really this casual when it comes to recognizing relatives? Don’t we need to go through some sort of procedure? A blood test, maybe?]","[He’s not even worried that I might be an undercover agent sent by someone else? He recognizes me just because I look like her and rolled my eyes once?]","Hearing these completely unrestrained thoughts, Su Zhen hugged her thigh even more tightly.","A blood test?","What did that crude trick, so easily tampered with, matter?","He could hear her thoughts!","Apart from his own flesh and blood, who else could share such a miraculous blood connection with him?","Even if she really was an impostor, she had warned him about the Qianji poison and saved his life. Either way, he had decided to acknowledge her as his daughter!","Although Su Yaoyao was ranting inwardly, her mind was already racing.","[Wait. Whether he’s mistaken or not, this is the Emperor of Dayuan!]","[The richest, most powerful man in the entire world, with an entire imperial treasury at his disposal!]","[If I latch onto him, why would I keep being the black-market boss? The whole world could become my source of money!]","[If I don’t seize this opportunity, I’ll regret it forever!]","With that thought, Su Yaoyao stuffed the solid-gold abacus in her hand into her arms.","She took a deep breath and swiftly adjusted her expression.","Then she forced two crystalline tears from her eyes and shouted with all the emotion she could muster:","“Father!”","The cry was clear and resonant, with enough feeling to make it echo through the entire hall.","Su Zhen’s whole body trembled. It was as though he had heard heavenly music, and his tears began to flow even more wildly.","“Ah! Good girl! My good girl!”","Father and daughter embraced each other tightly, patting each other on the back with perfect understanding.","In less than the time it took to drink a cup of tea, the most shameless father-daughter duo in history had officially been formed in the middle of a pool of blood.","Hearing his daughter calculating how to spend all his money, Su Zhen felt a strange sense of pride.","So what if his daughter liked money?","The imperial treasury was overflowing with it!","And if that wasn’t enough, he could always confiscate the estates of corrupt officials!","Su Zhen rose from the ground.","The sobbing old father vanished.","In his place stood the Tyrant, cold and ruthless, whose authority held sway over the four seas.","He swept out one great hand, his bloodstained sleeve cutting a fierce arc through the air.","“Deliver My imperial decree!”","The Imperial Guards immediately dropped to one knee in unison. The clashing of their armor rang through the hall.","“The operation to suppress the black market today was nothing more than a misunderstanding!”","“Effective immediately, the underground black market is no longer to be searched or seized. No one is to disturb it!”","Su Zhen’s powerful voice reverberated through the underground hall.","“Furthermore, from this day forward, this black market shall become the legal private property of the Crown Princess of Dayuan, exempt from all taxes!”","Crown Princess?!","Everyone drew in a sharp breath.","The black-market underlings had thought they were all going to be beheaded, with their entire families executed.","Yet in the blink of an eye, their boss had become the Crown Princess of Dayuan?","Didn’t that mean they were now the direct underlings of an imperial relative?!","The scar-faced man excitedly slapped himself across the face.","After confirming that he wasn’t dreaming, he immediately led the others in frantically kowtowing in the blood.","“Long live Your Highness! Long live Your Highness! Long, long live Your Highness!”","Su Yaoyao watched with satisfaction, her heart blooming with delight.","[This Tyrant of a father is surprisingly cooperative. He protected my business and even gave me a tax-exempt legal identity.]","[From now on, who in the capital will dare charge me protection fees?]","[Since that’s the case, I won’t stand on ceremony.]","Su Yaoyao hopped down from the armchair and swaggered over to the commander of the Imperial Guards.","She patted the commander’s priceless cold-iron linked armor.","“Now that the misunderstanding has been cleared up, we’re all on the same side.”","Su Yaoyao waved grandly toward the dozens of large redwood chests piled high with gold, silver, and jewels in the center of the hall.","“I’m going to acknowledge my ancestry and move into the imperial palace tonight.”","“There’s so much dowry—er, luggage. My men aren’t exactly built for heavy lifting, so they can’t carry it all.”","Su Yaoyao smiled sweetly at the dumbfounded commander of the Imperial Guards.","“Would you gentlemen mind setting aside your swords, spears, and halberds for a moment?”","“Please help Your Highness carry these chests back to the palace in one piece!”","The Imperial Guards were the elite of the elite, the royal force tasked with protecting the Emperor’s safety.","And now they had been ordered to do manual labor for a moving company?!","The commander of the Imperial Guards looked toward Su Zhen for help, hoping the Emperor would put a stop to Su Yaoyao’s outrageous behavior.","Instead, Su Zhen glared at him and barked, “Why are you looking at Me? The Crown Princess’s orders are My orders!”","“Didn’t you hear the Crown Princess? Get moving!”","“If even a single gold leaf of hers is damaged, I’ll chop off all your heads!”","The commander’s neck shrank back. He nearly burst into tears on the spot.","“Y-Yes, Your Majesty!”","The imposing Imperial Guards, who normally killed without blinking, all hung their weapons from their waists and began huffing and puffing as they hauled the heavy redwood chests.","“You, the tall one! Be careful with that chest of premium red coral. Even if we sold you, we couldn’t afford to compensate her if it broke!”","“And you! Keep those two chests of gold ingots covered tightly. Don’t let the wind blow any away!”","Su Yaoyao stood to one side like a wealthy landowner, pointing and issuing orders.","The scar-faced man and the other black-market underlings brought tea and refreshments as they watched the lofty Imperial Guards labor for their boss. The roughnecks were so delighted they nearly floated into the heavens.","Su Zhen stood with his arms crossed, watching his daughter’s money-loving ways.","The more he looked, the more he liked her.","Half an hour later, everything had been packed up.","The enormous procession departed from the filthy underground black market.","The Imperial Guards had transformed into heavily armored porters, hauling dozens of weighty chests.","Led by Su Zhen and Su Yaoyao, they swaggered toward the capital of Dayuan in full view of everyone.","Meanwhile, deep within the imperial palace of Dayuan...","Inside the resplendent Palace of Gathered Elegance, the brazier burned brightly, while the precious scent of ambergris incense curled through the air.","The most powerful woman in the imperial harem, Noble Consort Jing, reclined lazily on her chaise.","Her meticulously tended nail guards tapped against the rosewood table beside her as she waited for good news.","A trusted eunuch came tumbling into the hall, rolling and scrambling until he dropped to his knees with a thud.","“Your Highness! Your Highness, this is terrible!”","“What happened? Why are you making such a fuss? Have you no decorum?”","The Noble Consort did not even lift her eyelids. Her voice was coquettish yet cutting.","“His Majesty... His Majesty isn’t dead!”","The eunuch trembled all over, his voice quavering.","“Not only is he alive, Eunuch Li Fu was cleaved in two by His Majesty’s sword! The poison Eunuch Li Fu prepared wasn’t even needed!”","“What?!”","The Noble Consort sat bolt upright, her face drained of color.","“And that’s not all...”","The eunuch swallowed, his expression growing even more desperate as he continued.","“His Majesty recognized an illegitimate daughter at the black market. He’s now leading the Imperial Guards and making a grand spectacle of escorting that wild girl into the palace!”","“His Majesty even issued an edict before everyone, naming that wild girl the Crown Princess of Dayuan!”","As soon as the words left his mouth—","Bang!","The priceless Ru ware teacup beside the Noble Consort was swept to the floor by her hand and shattered into pieces.","Scalding tea splashed everywhere.","“The Crown Princess?!”","The Noble Consort’s face twisted with rage. Even her exquisite makeup could not conceal the venomous madness in her eyes.","She had fought her way through the imperial harem for years, exhausting every scheme and stratagem, yet had never even managed to come close to giving birth to a Crown Prince.","And now, some stray nobody picked up off the street actually dared to climb above her head and become the Crown Princess?!","The Noble Consort drew a deep breath, her chest rising and falling violently.","She rose to her feet, her sharp nail guards digging deeply into her palms. A chilling smile curled across her lips.","“A mongrel from the common folk thinks she’s worthy of becoming Crown Princess? Nanny Rong, prepare the carriage!”"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: The Imperial Palace Is Indeed a Great Place","paragraphs":["“Clang!”","“Clang!”","One heavy redwood chest after another slammed onto the gleaming golden-brick floor of Zhaoyang Hall.","The most lavish and spacious hall in the Great Yuan imperial palace looked like a dock in the middle of a war zone.","Sweat-soaked Imperial Guards stood in a long line, huffing and puffing as they carried goods into the main hall.","And standing in the very center, directing them, was a little girl barely tall enough to reach an adult’s waist.","Su Yaoyao wore the innocent face of an eight-year-old, but with her little hands planted on her hips, she had the air of a bandit inspecting her territory.","“You over there! Yes, you! Be careful when you set that chest down!”","“Those are exquisite glazed cups inside! If you chip even one, selling you to the Palace Bureau to become a eunuch wouldn’t be enough to cover the loss!”","Su Yaoyao shouted in her childish voice. Her practiced underworld slang and arrogant attitude were nothing like those of an eight-year-old.","Of course, inside her body lived the soul of an eighteen-year-old interstellar poison doctor and master mechanic.","As an interstellar laborer who had suffered through poverty, she had finally risen through the ranks. Naturally, she had to count every last penny!","The dozens of palace maids and eunuchs serving in the hall stood stiffly against the walls like wooden posts, scarcely daring to breathe.","They stared at the newly appointed Crown Princess in horror, their entire understanding of the world shattered.","According to rumor, Her Highness had been brought back by the emperor from the most chaotic underground black market in the capital.","Everyone had assumed she would be a timid, cowardly country girl who had never seen the world.","But once she entered the palace, it became clear that she had not come to be a caged songbird.","With all those bundles and chests, she looked for all the world like she had come to stock up on merchandise!","“Oh, is this thing made of pure gold?”","Su Yaoyao toddled over to a waist-high golden toad ornament in the corner of the hall.","Her eyes lit up. She reached out with her short, chubby hand and stroked its glittering surface.","Then, under the horrified gazes of every servant present, the Crown Princess rose onto her tiptoes, opened her mouth, and bit down hard on the golden toad’s back!","Crunch.","The metal warped.","Su Yaoyao let go and examined the row of tiny, clearly visible teeth marks on the toad’s back. Her peach-blossom eyes narrowed in satisfaction.","Real gold!","Extremely pure!","The little abacus in her mind began clacking away.","【Tsk, tsk, tsk. Tyrant Dad is certainly generous. Every ornament in Zhaoyang Hall is a hard currency.】","【Just this golden toad alone, melted down and made into gold bars, could probably buy half a street of shops.】","【The imperial palace really is a wonderful place. Gold everywhere you look. This trip is a huge profit!】","The palace maids and eunuchs stared at the imperial golden toad, now bearing a row of bite marks, their legs trembling violently.","If the emperor found out, the Crown Princess might be perfectly fine, but their heads certainly would not remain attached to their bodies!","After four full hours of chaos, the Imperial Guards had finally transported every last possession from the black market.","Su Yaoyao waved them away, dismissing the Imperial Guard commander like a laborer who had finished the job.","She turned around and looked toward the ornate canopy bed at the far end of the hall.","The bed had been carved from a single piece of century-old golden-thread nanmu, and its thick mattress was covered with snow-marten fur from the Western Regions.","It looked impossibly soft and radiated an alluring scent of wealth.","An eight-year-old body really did tire easily.","Su Yaoyao stretched luxuriantly.","She kicked off her little boots and was just about to fling herself onto the fragrant bed and enjoy a good, well-earned rest.","Suddenly, a sharp, piercing eunuch’s announcement rang out from beyond the hall.","“Noble Consort Jing has arrived!”","Su Yaoyao froze mid-pounce.","She knitted her little brows and pursed her lips unhappily.","【Noble Consort Jing? The old hag who rules the entire harem and whose informant eunuch just died?】","【I haven’t even touched my bed yet, and someone’s already come here to offer up their head?】","A crisp jingle of ornaments rang out as a strong, pungent wave of face powder swept into Zhaoyang Hall.","Noble Consort Jing entered with an imposing air, surrounded by a group of palace maids and senior matrons.","She wore a gorgeous bright-red peony palace gown, and the golden hairpins dangling from her head swayed violently with every step.","Although she wore a smile, it did not reach her eyes. Instead, her expression held a coldness sharpened by barely contained resentment.","In the imperial harem, Noble Consort Jing had thrown her weight around for many years.","She had long regarded the empress’s position as already hers for the taking.","And then, today, an eight-year-old brat had appeared out of nowhere and climbed above her, becoming the Crown Princess!","How could she possibly swallow such an insult?","“Oh my, so this is the Crown Princess?”","Noble Consort Jing walked to the center of the hall and looked down at Su Yaoyao.","When she saw that exquisite little face—one that resembled the late empress’s by at least seventy percent—the jealousy in her eyes nearly burst into flames.","“This consort pays her respects to Your Highness.”","Noble Consort Jing gave a perfunctory curtsy, barely bending her knees before straightening again.","She covered her nose and mouth with a handkerchief and cast a disdainful glance at the redwood chests that had yet to be cleared away.","“As expected of someone from the common folk. She’s never seen the world.”","“How dare she bring all this junk into Zhaoyang Hall? It reeks of the shabby, vulgar air of the marketplace.”","The moment Noble Consort Jing opened her mouth, she was already dripping with sarcasm.","Counting on Su Yaoyao being a child who could not understand the hidden meaning behind her words, she made no effort to show restraint.","The palace maids and eunuchs in the hall all lowered their heads, not daring even to breathe too loudly.","When immortals fought, ordinary people suffered.","Everyone had witnessed Noble Consort Jing’s methods in the harem.","Su Yaoyao stood barefoot on the golden-brick floor. She tilted her little head and blinked her clear, luminous eyes at Noble Consort Jing.","【The gold hairpin on that old hag’s head is quite heavy. It must weigh at least three ounces of gold.】","【The pearls on her clothes aren’t bad either. I could probably sell them for a pretty penny after prying them off.】","【It’s just a shame that her mouth stinks so badly. It’s as if she’s been eating dead rats.】","Seeing that Su Yaoyao did not respond, Noble Consort Jing assumed the little girl had been frightened senseless by her imposing manner.","The mockery at the corners of her mouth deepened as she let out a cold laugh.","“Now that Your Highness has entered the palace, you represent the dignity of the Great Yuan Kingdom.”","“That wild, uncivilized behavior you displayed in the black market must be changed completely. Otherwise, you’ll cause trouble in the future and bring shame upon His Majesty.”","Noble Consort Jing turned and pulled forward an imposing old woman with a burly build and a face full of flesh.","The woman had high cheekbones and narrow, triangular eyes. One look was enough to tell that she was vicious and ruthless.","“His Majesty is busy with state affairs and has no time to educate Your Highness.”","“As the head of the imperial harem, it is only natural that I should relieve His Majesty of this burden.”","Noble Consort Jing pointed at the old woman with a false smile plastered across her face.","“This is Nanny Gui, the person in the palace who understands the rules best.”","“From today onward, Nanny Gui will remain in Zhaoyang Hall and personally teach Your Highness palace etiquette.”","“If Your Highness makes any mistakes, Nanny Gui may act on my behalf and discipline you. So please don’t complain about hardship.”","It was called instruction, but in truth it was torture—and an attempt to plant a spy at her side.","The tricks of the imperial harem were nothing new to eighteen-year-old Su Yaoyao. She had seen them countless times in costume dramas.","She still said nothing. She simply watched Noble Consort Jing perform, a pure smile curving her lips.","Receiving Noble Consort Jing’s meaningful glance, Nanny Gui immediately understood.","She strode forward and loomed over Su Yaoyao.","“Your Highness, the first rule in the palace is that status and seniority must be respected.”","Nanny Gui’s voice was rough and unpleasant, like a night bird shrieking in the dark.","“Her Highness the Noble Consort is your elder. Your Highness ought to pay your respects with a formal bow.”","As she spoke, Nanny Gui extended a large hand as rough as dry tree bark and pressed it toward Su Yaoyao’s tender shoulder.","She used tremendous force, clearly intent on forcing the girl to her knees and making a spectacle of her!","The palace attendants around them drew in sharp breaths, yet no one dared step forward to intervene.","Nanny Gui’s hand was just about to land on that tiny shoulder.","At the bend in the corridor outside Zhaoyang Hall,","Su Zhen had just finished rapidly reviewing memorials in the Imperial Study and hurried over, his heart brimming with delight at the thought of seeing his beloved daughter.","He stopped in his tracks.","The smile on his face suddenly darkened, as though rainwater might drip from it.","At the very instant Nanny Gui made her move,","an inner voice, excited to the point of madness—as though it wanted to devour someone—rang out in Su Zhen’s mind..."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Fuck Your Palace Rules","paragraphs":["The heavy, bronze-clad wooden doors of Zhaoyang Hall were only inches away.","A murderous intent surged through Su Zhen’s deep-set eyes.","He raised his right leg, clad in black dragon boots, as the true qi in his dantian began circulating at full force.","He was ready to kick the doors to pieces, storm inside, and chop that old witch who didn’t know her place into minced meat.","How dare she bully the precious daughter he had only just reclaimed?","She was clearly tired of living!","But just as the sole of his boot was half an inch from the door—","A familiar, crisp voice filled with barely restrained excitement exploded in his mind.","[Well, well? The old witch has come to deliver her own head!]","[I was just worrying about where to find a suitable test subject for the Smiling Half-Step Madness I concocted in my space!]","[And now someone has actually come running to offer herself up? What a saintly benefactor!]","Su Zhen’s right leg, which had been poised to strike with the force of thunder, froze in midair.","Smiling Half-Step Madness?","What strange and unusual poison was this—something he had never heard of or even seen before?","He silently withdrew his foot and placed it back on the ground.","The overwhelming fury and icy killing intent on Su Zhen’s face vanished in the blink of an eye.","In their place was an indescribable anticipation, mixed with the eager delight of someone ready to watch a good show.","He turned around and glared fiercely at the hidden guards behind him, who were just preparing to draw their blades.","“Go. Bring me a little stool. And keep your movements light. Anyone who makes a sound will be executed.”","The newly appointed chief eunuch was so shocked that his jaw nearly hit the floor. He didn’t dare utter a single word.","He scrambled to a corner, brought back an exquisitely crafted wooden folding stool, and set it down.","The tyrant of the ages, the iron-fisted emperor of the Great Yuan Empire, the man whose name struck terror into the hearts of all beneath heaven—","sat obediently beneath the window of his daughter’s bedchamber.","He carefully poked a hole in the expensive Korean paper covering the window.","Squinting one eye, Su Zhen leaned toward the opening, eagerly preparing to enjoy the spectacle.","Inside Zhaoyang Hall, the atmosphere had dropped to freezing point.","Nanny Gui’s rough hands were clamped tightly around Su Yaoyao’s tender shoulders.","Noble Consort Jing sat gracefully to one side in a carved huanghuali-wood chair.","She held a cup of freshly brewed pre-Qingming Longjing tea, gently blowing away the rising steam.","“Your Highness, you mustn’t blame this palace for being too strict with you.”","Noble Consort Jing’s voice was soft and melodious.","“The imperial family values rules and decorum above all else. You grew up wandering among commoners and have picked up all the crude habits of the streets.”","“If you don’t properly learn the etiquette of kneeling and kowtowing, how will you face the ancestors of the Great Yuan Empire in the future?”","“And how will you ever repay His Majesty’s boundless grace in bringing you back to the palace?”","“This palace is doing all of this for your own good. You must understand my painstaking concern for you.”","Noble Consort Jing took a delicate sip of tea, the corners of her lips curling into a mocking, triumphant smile.","The palace maids and eunuchs around them exchanged looks, each determined to protect themselves by staying out of trouble.","In the inner palace, moral coercion was always the sharpest blade—a weapon that killed without spilling blood.","Once rules and the ancestors were invoked as two towering mountains, even the emperor had to give way.","Let alone a country girl with no roots or backing.","At this, Nanny Gui’s arm muscles tensed. She increased the pressure of her grip, intending to force the little girl’s knees onto the golden-brick floor.","But who could have imagined that Su Yaoyao’s seemingly delicate body would writhe like a slippery loach?","Using the most advanced close-combat footwork of the interstellar age, she slipped free from Nanny Gui’s grasp.","Nanny Gui had put too much force into it and suddenly lost her balance.","Her fat, heavy body pitched straight forward, nearly sending her sprawling face-first onto the floor.","“How dare you! You actually dodged!”","Seeing this, Noble Consort Jing slammed her teacup onto the table, her expression darkening.","“You have no respect for your elders! Nanny Gui, teach her a proper lesson!”","Su Yaoyao stood all alone in the middle of the hall, her little head lowered.","Her thin shoulders began to tremble faintly.","Everyone assumed that she had finally been frightened into tears by the consort’s thunderous fury.","Su Yaoyao lifted her head, sending her long black hair whipping wildly around her face.","Her round, innocent features twisted out of shape!","She rolled her eyes upward, revealing a large expanse of terrifying white, and stared fixedly at the ceiling.","Then she opened her mouth and unleashed a sharp, ear-piercing shriek devoid of all reason.","“Ahhhhhhh!”","It was like the mournful wail of a ghost in the dead of night.","Nanny Gui, who had only just regained her footing, was so startled by the sudden scream that she staggered back three steps.","Noble Consort Jing’s hand shook, and scalding tea splashed across her luxurious peony-embroidered palace gown.","“You want to morally blackmail me?!”","Su Yaoyao screamed at the top of her lungs, the muscles in her face twitching grotesquely from the effort.","She thrust both hands into her hair and clawed at it wildly, turning it into a tangled bird’s nest.","“Ah! I have no morals! You can’t blackmail me!!!”","She hopped and leaped around like a madwoman, stomping both feet against the golden bricks until the entire hall seemed to shake.","“Rules? What the hell are rules? I am the rules!”","“You want me to kneel? Believe me, I’ll kneel at your family’s ancestral grave right now!”","“Ahhhhh! There are ghosts! I saw the late emperor coming with the Black and White Impermanence to claim your lives!”","She flailed her arms and legs, every movement exaggerated to the extreme. She looked exactly like a madwoman possessed by an evil spirit.","Zhaoyang Hall fell into deathly silence.","Ahhhhh! This was like the scene of a high-security psychiatric patient escaping from an asylum!","The carefully maintained complexion of Noble Consort Jing turned as pale as paper.","All the dignity and nobility she had worked so hard to preserve shattered into pieces before Su Yaoyao’s madness.","“She’s insane! This bastard is completely insane!”","Noble Consort Jing pointed at Su Yaoyao. The finger bearing a pure-gold nail guard trembled violently, and her voice was filled with panic.","“Quick! Restrain her! Gag her! Don’t let her keep shouting like this!”","Nanny Gui and several broad-shouldered, burly palace maids gritted their teeth and charged forward.","They spread their arms, attempting to subdue the crazed little girl through sheer numbers.","But instead of retreating even half a step, Su Yaoyao abruptly stopped screaming.","She lowered her head and let out a deep, chilling laugh.","As the palace maids rushed toward her, Su Yaoyao charged straight at them like a frenzied young beast.","Her formidable physique erupted with speed that did not belong to a child.","Like a gust of wind, she slipped around Nanny Gui and dashed to the seat in front of Noble Consort Jing.","Su Yaoyao reached out with both little hands and gripped the edge of the heavy rosewood tea table before Noble Consort Jing.","“To hell with your palace rules!”","With a furious roar, terrifying strength exploded from her slender arms.","She heaved upward and sent the entire heavy tea table flying into the air!","Crash!","Scalding tea, delicate white porcelain, and several plates of exquisite pastries scattered overhead, transforming into a chaotic downpour that rained straight down upon Noble Consort Jing.","Noble Consort Jing shrieked in terror and hurriedly raised both arms to shield her face.","Amid the tea and shards of broken porcelain swirling through the air—","the little hand hidden inside Su Yaoyao’s oversized sleeve flicked inconspicuously.","A fine, colorless, odorless powder dissolved into the air.","Carried by the gust stirred up when the table was overturned, it drifted toward Noble Consort Jing, Nanny Gui, and the palace maids around them.","The poison took effect instantly!"]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: The Imperial Consort Has Been Possessed by an Evil Spirit","paragraphs":["A colorless, odorless powder.","It scattered forward amid the tea that flew through the air, scalding hot, along with shards of shattered porcelain.","Caught completely off guard, Noble Consort Jing, Nanny Gui, and the several fierce palace maids who had charged forward like wolves and tigers were engulfed by the dust.","The powder entered their open mouths and rushed through their nostrils with every rapid breath, dissolving into their bloodstream.","Noble Consort Jing flailed her arms in terror, trying to block the tea splashing toward her.","Fury blazed in her chest. She was just about to put on the full authority of a noble consort and order this ignorant little wretch beaten to death.","But before the vicious command could leave her lips, an eerie coolness shot straight through her nasal passages and into the crown of her head. An invisible hand seized control of her brain and nerves.","Noble Consort Jing felt a thunderous “buzz” explode inside her skull.","Her exquisite features, twisted by rage and terror, froze in place.","Then an impulse that reason could not suppress erupted from her organs like a volcano.","Her tightly pressed red lips began to twitch violently.","A moment later, against her will, the corners of her mouth shot upward at a bizarre angle, pulling wildly toward her ears!","“Geh... gehehehe...”","A deep, strange sound, like an old goose being strangled, rolled from Noble Consort Jing’s throat.","The laughter grew louder and more unrestrained, breaking completely through the confines of her throat.","Soon it became a barbell-like roar that echoed throughout the entire Zhaoyang Hall!","“Ha ha ha ha ha! Gehehehehe!”","Noble Consort Jing lowered the arms she had raised to shield her face while emitting ear-splitting, uncontrollable laughter.","It was not only her. Nanny Gui, who had charged at the very front moments ago in an attempt to restrain Su Yaoyao, as well as the broad-shouldered, fierce-looking palace maids, had all joined the mad chorus of laughter as if someone had struck their laughing pressure points.","Zhaoyang Hall filled with the demonic sounds of “gehehehe” and “ha ha ha ha,” drilling straight into the ears.","But this was only the first stage of the effects of Laughing Madness Powder.","As the most popular prank drug of the interstellar era, its most terrifying feature was its ability to control the body’s motor nerves!","“Ha ha ha... My legs... What’s wrong with my legs... Ha ha ha!”","Noble Consort Jing realized in utter horror that her body had stopped obeying her as well.","Her feet, clad in expensive Shu brocade platform shoes, took a large involuntary step forward, making the ornaments in her hair jingle wildly.","Then her left foot crossed over, followed by a slide of her right.","Her waist, cinched impossibly narrow by her corset, began twisting violently to an invisible, frenzied beat!","Two twists to the left, two twists to the right, followed by an exaggerated circle drawn with her hips.","Her arms, adorned with pure-gold hollowed-out nail guards, flailed in the air like seaweed whipping about in a gale.","What a pose! What footwork!","What a breathtakingly sultry rhythm!","Nanny Gui was not about to be outdone.","Normally, she wore the stern, expressionless face of a corpse. As the strict and hidebound nanny feared throughout the Six Palaces, she was now baring a huge mouth, laughing so hard that even her back teeth were visible.","With both hands planted on her barrel-thick waist, her enormous backside swayed wildly from side to side. She danced with ten times more enthusiasm than Noble Consort Jing!","“Ha ha ha ha ha! Your Ladyship... This old servant can’t stop... Ha ha ha ha ha!”","Still laughing maniacally, Nanny Gui advanced with a devilish dance step and slammed into Noble Consort Jing.","The second stage of the drug’s effects: the period of frenzied physical interaction!","Knocked off balance, Noble Consort Jing’s eyes turned bloodshot, and tears of humiliation streamed down her face.","Yet a bright, twisted grin remained plastered across her features.","“Gehehehe! You blind old hag, how dare you bump into me... Ha ha ha!”","Still producing uncontrollable barbell-like laughter, Noble Consort Jing reached out with both hands.","She seized Nanny Gui’s meticulously arranged, old-fashioned bun and yanked hard, tearing out a large handful of hair streaked with gray.","Nanny Gui cried out in pain, but the laughter spilling from her mouth only grew louder, tears and snot streaming down her face.","She refused to be outdone. Reaching back, she grabbed Noble Consort Jing by the collar of her splendid scarlet peony court robe.","“Ha ha ha! Your Ladyship, forgive me! This old servant can’t control these hands... Ha ha ha ha!”","In the very center of the main hall, on the golden brick floor, the two women danced an eye-searing square dance while beating each other without the slightest regard for their dignity!","The phoenix-gold hairpin worth a fortune was torn from Noble Consort Jing’s head, leaving her black hair in disarray.","Her expensive scarlet court robe was ripped open by Nanny Gui, exposing the white garment beneath.","Nanny Gui’s old face was scored by a long bloody scratch from Noble Consort Jing’s razor-sharp gold nail guards.","The several palace maids who had been caught in the powder could not control themselves either. They joined the melee, grabbing one another’s hair and tearing at each other’s clothes. They rolled together across the smooth golden bricks, laughing wildly as they thrashed about.","No matter how fiercely they struck one another, how painfully they pulled, or how badly they tore their clothes, every one of them wore a feverish smile while continuously shrieking the deranged laughter of “gehehehe.”","It was ten thousand times more terrifying than a horde of demons dancing in the underworld!","Inside Zhaoyang Hall, the palace maids and eunuchs who had avoided the powder were utterly stunned.","Everyone stood rooted to the spot as if frozen by a spell, their bodies cold from head to toe.","One young eunuch dropped the horsetail whisk in his hand and did not even notice.","Some of the palace maids clapped both hands tightly over their mouths, their eyeballs nearly bulging from their sockets.","This...","Was this really Noble Consort Jing, who stood high above them all, dignified and imposing, wielding authority over the Six Palaces?!","Was this really Nanny Gui, who beat and berated servants at the slightest provocation and constantly lectured everyone about rules and propriety?!","The way they looked now—with their hair disheveled, clothes in disarray, rolling around on the floor and laughing hysterically—","They were even more disgraceful than common thugs throwing a tantrum!","“Riiip!”","The sharp sound of tearing fabric suddenly rang out.","In the midst of her fierce struggle with Nanny Gui, Noble Consort Jing’s body sank downward.","Her two legs, which had never undergone any flexibility training, were forcibly driven by the drug’s effects.","On the hard, icy golden brick floor, they actually split into a perfect straight line!","“Ha ha ha ha ha! It hurts so much! My inner thighs are going to snap... Gehehehehe!”","Noble Consort Jing’s tears shot out from the pain. Her face contorted, yet the brilliant smile remained fixed in place, and the laughter would not stop.","She sat on the floor in a brutally painful split, waving her arms to the rhythm.","The physical damage was immense. The humiliation was even worse.","The mastermind behind this earth-shaking farce was the eight-year-old Her Highness Crown Princess Su Yaoyao.","She clung to one of the golden nanmu pillars in the center of the hall, trembling from head to toe.","Her delicate, doll-like face was hidden behind the pillar, revealing only a pair of clear, bright eyes.","The mischief and glee in them were practically overflowing.","[Tsk, tsk, tsk. Their square dancing has absolutely no sense of rhythm, and their arms and legs are completely out of sync.]","[Though I have to admit, that split was impressive. This enhanced Frenzied Dance formula really is something else!]","[Old witch, this is what you get for lecturing me about rules. Today, I’ll teach you what “rules” really mean!]","Su Yaoyao savagely critiqued the scene in her mind. But on the surface, she was nothing more than a frightened little victim.","She drew in a deep breath and summoned two crystal-clear tears.","Her eyes reddened, and she threw back her head, unleashing a shriek a hundred times more piercing than the one before.","“There’s a ghost!!!”","The child’s sharp, sobbing cry pierced through the chaos of Zhaoyang Palace and soared into the heavens.","While pretending to be utterly terrified and shrinking behind a pillar, Su Yaoyao pointed with a trembling little finger at Noble Consort Jing, who was doing the splits on the floor and laughing hysterically.","“Waaah! Her Ladyship Noble Consort Jing has been possessed by an evil ghost!”","“She’s gone mad! She’s going to eat people! She’s been possessed!”","“Help! Somebody save me! Father, save me!”","Su Yaoyao cried as though her heart were breaking, tears streaming down her face like pear blossoms in the rain. She looked as if she had truly been scared witless by some evil spirit.","Her expression of utter terror, combined with the madwoman in the center of the hall who was laughing wildly while fighting with someone else, made the resplendent Zhaoyang Palace look like a living hell.","The palace maids and eunuchs who had been scared stiff shuddered when they heard Su Yaoyao cry out that Noble Consort Jing had been possessed by an evil ghost.","That was right!","If she hadn’t been possessed—if she hadn’t been taken over by an evil ghost—how could the noble consort, who had always cared most about preserving her dignity, possibly do something so outrageously absurd?!","“There are ghosts! Her Ladyship has been possessed!”","Several of the younger palace servants could take no more. They screamed in terror and collapsed to the floor.","Zhaoyang Palace descended into unparalleled chaos and panic.","Wild laughter, the sound of clothes being torn, the palace servants’ cries of alarm, and a little girl’s heart-wrenching sobs all blended together in a racket that set everyone’s nerves on edge.","While wiping away tears that did not exist, Su Yaoyao pricked up her ears and listened to the commotion outside.","That should be enough.","The atmosphere had been built up to just the right point.","The spectator outside, who had been watching the show for so long, ought to make his grand entrance now and bring everything to a perfect close.","Just as the lingering echo of Su Yaoyao’s cry of “Father, save me!” was still circling beneath the rafters of the great hall—","“Bang!!!”","The extraordinarily thick, bronze-plated doors of Zhaoyang Palace were kicked open from outside with tremendous force!","The impact sent both door panels crashing against the walls with a deafening boom.","The cold wind outside, carrying the bone-chilling majesty of an emperor, swept through the hall.","Su Zhen strode across the high threshold.","Dressed in a dark-black dragon robe, with the Longquan sword at his waist, he was tall and imposing, as though a god had descended from the heavens.","Yet this ruler of Dayuan, who had just been poking a hole through the window and enthusiastically watching the entire spectacle from outside—","had a handsome, peerless face so dark it seemed capable of dripping black water.","His eyes burned with blazing fury as he stared at the painfully absurd scene in the middle of the hall.","But upon closer inspection, one would notice that the lips of this Tyrant, pressed into a straight line, were twitching violently."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: So Biased It Reaches the Pacific Ocean","paragraphs":["Su Zhen had barely stepped through the doors, without even having time to put on the full display of an emperor’s fury, when a tiny figure shot out from behind the golden-thread nanmu pillar in the center of the hall like a cannonball from the barrel of a gun.","“Waaah! Father Emperor! Save me!”","Su Yaoyao’s eight-year-old legs pumped furiously as she tore across the polished golden-brick floor with an utterly reckless swagger.","When she was half a meter away from Su Zhen, she expertly let her knees buckle.","Riding the momentum, she slid forward and latched onto Su Zhen’s leg, hugging the one clad in black dragon boots without missing by an inch.","Her exquisitely delicate little face was buried hard in the expensive fabric of his dragon robe.","With her eyes squeezed shut, Su Yaoyao threw back her head and wailed at the top of her lungs, as if her heart had been torn apart.","The thunder was deafening, but there was hardly any rain. Not a single tear fell.","While no one could see, she secretly rubbed her reddened eyes—reddened from pretending to be pitiful—against the dragon robe.","[That scared the life out of me! This old witch is a dancing genius!]","[My titanium-alloy eyes are practically blinded!]","[Father Emperor, you have to stand up for me! The emotional-distress compensation alone should be at least a hundred or two hundred thousand taels, don’t you think?]","Her bright, cheerful thoughts, brimming with undisguised gloating, crashed into Su Zhen’s mind.","The taut line of Su Zhen’s jaw nearly gave way.","Forcing down the corners of his mouth, which were trying desperately to rise, he lowered his head and looked at the little head that was pretending to tremble against his leg.","“Don’t be afraid, don’t be afraid. Father Emperor is here. No one can hurt you.”","Su Zhen extended his broad hand and patted Su Yaoyao’s fluffy head soothingly twice.","Then he raised his head.","His deep, icy eyes swept toward the center of the hall.","Noble Consort Jing was still sitting on the cold golden-brick floor in a particularly gruesome split.","The once-luxurious crimson peony palace dress had been torn into strips of rags.","Her elegant coiffure was in complete disarray, and several strands of hair were still clenched in Nanny Gui’s hand.","When she saw the emperor descend like a god from the heavens, a burst of wild delight flared in the depths of Noble Consort Jing’s despairing eyes.","The emperor was here!","Her savior had finally arrived!","She would make her complaint!","She would appeal directly to the emperor!","She would make him see just what kind of bold, cruel demon this wild child picked up from the black market truly was!","Noble Consort Jing trembled all over with excitement, desperately trying to wipe the strange smile from her face.","She wanted to replace it with an aggrieved, helpless expression, like a pear blossom streaked with tears.","Her trembling hand reached toward Su Zhen in desperation.","“Your... Your Majesty...”","Noble Consort Jing opened her mouth, ready to accuse Su Yaoyao.","But the instant her vocal cords vibrated—","“Hahahahaha... Your Majesty, save me... geese, geese, geese!”","A loud, barbell-like burst of manic laughter erupted from her throat.","Noble Consort Jing’s eyes widened in terror.","No!","She didn’t want to laugh!","Her inner thighs were aching terribly, and her scalp hurt from being yanked.","She wanted to cry!","“Your Majesty... I didn’t... Hahahaha... It was her... geese, geese, geese!”","Noble Consort Jing shook her head frantically. Tears mixed with her smeared cosmetics, washing two muddy streaks down her face.","No matter how hard she tried, every word she spoke was interrupted by her crazed laughter.","To anyone watching, it looked exactly like she was provoking the emperor.","Beside her, Nanny Gui was tugging on the consort’s hair while rolling around on the floor, laughing hysterically.","“Hahahaha... Long live Your Majesty... This old servant can’t stop... Hahahaha!”","Su Zhen looked down at the mistress and servant from above, his eyes devoid of warmth.","He gave a cold snort.","“How dare you, Noble Consort!”","Su Zhen’s voice was deep, dignified, and commanding.","“As the head of the imperial harem, you should be dignified and virtuous, serving as an example to the entire harem!”","“And yet here you are, in front of the Crown Princess’s residence, with your clothes in disarray, disgracing yourself and acting like a madwoman!”","“You even brought a servant here to dance like a demon and make a racket. What kind of conduct is this?”","Su Zhen stepped forward, his imperial authority bearing down like Mount Tai.","“Are you trying to show defiance toward Me? Or did you deliberately barge in on My precious daughter?!”","Noble Consort Jing was struck dumb as if by a thunderbolt.","She had been poisoned by that little demon!","Could the emperor not see that she had been forced into this?!","“No... It wasn’t... Hahahaha... I’ve been wronged, Your Majesty... geese, geese, geese!”","Noble Consort Jing waved her hands frantically, trying to explain.","But Su Zhen did not give her the chance to plead her case. He pronounced judgment on the spot.","“Wronged? I saw everything with My own eyes. You were laughing so wildly—where is the injustice in that?”","“The Crown Princess has only just returned to the palace. She is young and timid.”","“As her elder, instead of showing her care, you came here to play the ghost and frighten her into fleeing in panic!”","The more Su Zhen spoke, the harsher he became, painting Noble Consort Jing as though she had committed one of the ten unforgivable crimes.","Hearing the words “young and timid” and “fleeing in panic,” Su Yaoyao, who was clinging to Su Zhen’s leg, nearly burst out laughing.","[Oh my goodness, my tyrant father is such a phenomenal actor!]","[His talent for twisting right and wrong and his eloquence at calling a deer a horse are incredible. What a waste that he isn’t writing storybooks!]","[This is favoritism on a continental scale! I love it!]","Hearing his daughter’s praise, Su Zhen straightened his back even further.","Naturally. If he was going to protect his child, then he would protect her to the very end. What need was there to talk about reason?","Throughout the world, the emperor’s word was the greatest reason of all!","Su Yaoyao poked half of her little head out and cooperated with Su Zhen’s performance.","“Father Emperor, Noble Consort Jing is so scary. She even tried to hit me. Boo-hoo-hoo...”","“She also said I wasn’t worthy of being the Crown Princess and that she was going to teach me a lesson...”","Su Yaoyao pretended to cry while continuing to hand Su Zhen ammunition in her thoughts.","[Father Emperor, this old witch bullied me. You can’t just let her off.]","[I heard that her Palace of Gathering Beauty is piled high with gold, silver, and precious treasures, all gifts from people trying to curry favor with her.]","[Those red corals and luminous pearls tributed from the Western Regions are all stored there, too.]","[Since she frightened me, taking a few things to calm my nerves shouldn’t be too much to ask, right?]","Not too much at all! It was perfectly reasonable!","Su Zhen silently nodded in agreement.","Although father and daughter exchanged no words, they had already completed the most harmonious joint operation of plundering the plunderers.","Su Zhen’s gaze sharpened as he delivered the final verdict.","“By My decree!”","“Noble Consort Jing has disgraced herself before the Crown Princess and shown disrespect toward her. Her virtue is wanting, and she is unfit to serve as an example to the imperial harem!”","“Effective immediately, she is stripped of her authority to oversee the harem and confined to the Palace of Gathering Beauty for three months of reflection!”","“Without My permission, no one is to visit her!”","The moment these words were spoken, Noble Consort Jing felt as if five thunderbolts had struck her at once. Her vision went black.","Confined to the Palace of Gathering Beauty for three months?!","What difference was that from being sent to the cold palace?!","Once she lost the power in her hands, wouldn’t the consorts she had oppressed all this time tear her apart?","“Your Majesty... Hahahaha... No! Please don’t! I know I was wrong... geese, geese, geese!”","Noble Consort Jing reached out desperately, trying to grab Su Zhen’s leg.","But the commander of the Imperial Guards kicked her away.","“She’s still laughing? It seems Noble Consort Jing has no intention of repenting!”","Su Zhen coldly brushed off his sleeve.","“The Crown Princess has suffered a terrible fright today and been wounded in both body and spirit.”","“To calm the Crown Princess’s nerves and punish Noble Consort Jing...”","“Guards! Proceed to the Palace of Gathering Beauty at once!”","“Take every piece of gold, silver, jade, antique, and painting in Noble Consort Jing’s palace, as well as those rare treasures tributed from the Western Regions.”","“Leave not a single item behind. Clear the entire palace!”","“Move everything to the Crown Princess’s residence and bestow it all upon Her Highness for her amusement!”","Those words were the final straw that broke the camel’s back.","They struck Noble Consort Jing right in the heart.","Empty out the Palace of Accumulated Elegance?!","That was everything she had amassed over more than a decade in the imperial palace through painstaking scheming, deceit, and ruthless plunder!","Priceless jewelry and rare treasures so extraordinary that she had never even dared to touch them.","And now she was expected to give them all to this little wretch who had ruined her?!","That was a thousand times more agonizing than killing her!","Noble Consort Jing was overwhelmed by rage. Her chest heaved violently.","The immense despair and humiliation, the excruciating pain of her torn muscles, and the forced laughter brought on by the drug—","Her body could no longer endure such torment.","“Ha-ha-ha-ha... My fortune... My money... Guh-guh-guh... Ah!”","Noble Consort Jing rolled her eyes dramatically.","Amid her shrill, deranged laughter, her head lolled to the side, and she fainted on the golden floor tiles.","Even unconscious, the muscles in her face continued to twitch from time to time, pulling her features into an eerie smile.","“Master! Master has fainted!”","Several palace maids who had been affected by the drug laughed hysterically as they crawled and stumbled toward Noble Consort Jing.","“Take them away! Throw them all into the Palace of Accumulated Elegance. Don’t let them stand here and offend the Crown Princess!”","Su Zhen waved his hand in disgust, as if shooing away flies.","The Imperial Guards immediately stepped forward.","They paid no heed to the propriety between men and women. Grabbing Noble Consort Jing and Nanny Gui by the ankles, they dragged them out of Zhaoyang Palace like dead dogs.","Their shrill, maniacal laughter grew more distant, until it finally vanished altogether.","The chaotic Zhaoyang Palace at last returned to peace.","Several quick-witted eunuchs hurried forward and cleaned up the water and broken porcelain scattered across the floor as swiftly as possible.","Su Yaoyao stood in the middle of the great hall, gazing at the spacious, spotless palace.","Then she thought about all the belongings from the Palace of Accumulated Elegance that would soon be delivered to her.","Her beautiful peach-blossom eyes curved into two adorable little crescents.","The imperial harem?","No, no, no!","This was her cash machine!","Just then, Su Yaoyao’s inner voice rang out cheerfully in Su Zhen’s mind once again."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Those high officials of the previous dynasty should have had more fat to skim off, right","paragraphs":["The threshold of Zhaoyang Palace had practically been worn flat tonight.","Under the Tyrant Dad’s threat of death, the Imperial Guards had unleashed astonishing efficiency.","It had taken less than half an hour.","Everything in the Palace of Gathered Elegance that could reflect light or fetch a decent price had been hauled away by those ravenous Imperial Guards.","One after another, enormous redwood chests were carried into Zhaoyang Palace like water flowing through a channel.","The spacious, empty hall was soon piled high, transformed into a glittering miniature treasury.","“Careful, careful! Set down that three-foot-tall jade Guanyin gently!”","“And those two luminous pearls presented by the Western Regions—put them in a brocade box. Don’t scratch or bump them!”","Su Yaoyao darted through the mountains of gold and silver like an agile little monkey.","Cradling a heavy solid-gold Maitreya Buddha in her arms, she beamed more brightly than the statue itself.","The most luxurious canopy bed in the Great Yuan Kingdom was covered in thick stacks of banknotes and ingots of gold.","Su Yaoyao threw herself onto it and rolled happily through the mountain of money, letting out a satisfied sigh.","Clink, clank.","The gold and silver ingots collided, producing the most delightful, crisp sound in the world.","Su Yaoyao pulled a pure-gold abacus from her robes and began working the beads at lightning speed.","The beads blurred, making a crisp pitter-patter.","“Two coral branches from the Eastern Sea—valued at eighty thousand taels of silver.”","“A pair of top-grade mutton-fat jade ruyi—valued at forty thousand taels.”","“Add these scattered gold leaves, silver ingots, and these several boxes of pearls the size of thumbs...”","The more Su Yaoyao calculated, the brighter her eyes became. Her lovely, almond-shaped eyes practically turned into copper coins.","She was rich!","This time, she was truly rich!","In her previous life, during the interstellar era, she had risked her life every day to obtain materials for military research and development, fighting mutated beasts for territory.","In this life, she had transmigrated into the leader of a black-market syndicate, still spending every day fighting alongside her underlings and racking her brains just to scrape together a modest fortune.","But after arriving at the imperial palace of the Great Yuan Kingdom, everything had changed!","She didn’t need to bleed or sweat, or lift a finger herself.","All she had to do was pretend to be delicate, scatter a handful of colorless, odorless prank powder, and wail a couple of times.","A fortune from heaven had practically grown legs and run straight into her pockets!","Su Yaoyao grabbed a handful of gold leaves and tossed them into the air, watching them fall like golden rain.","【Money from the imperial palace is so easy to earn!】","【It’s so much faster than collecting protection fees and fighting over territory in the black market!】","【And I’ve even got a Tyrant Dad who follows my every command as my backer.】","【A sure-win business with enormous returns!】","Her crisp, cheerful inner voice drifted through the air of Zhaoyang Palace.","Outside the palace’s half-shut, intricately carved window stood Su Zhen, who had been preparing to leave.","His dark dragon robes fluttered in the night breeze.","Upon hearing his daughter’s heartfelt praise, a proud smile appeared on the face of the man who had been an iceberg for ten thousand years.","He couldn’t help raising his chin arrogantly.","Naturally!","He was the emperor of the Great Yuan Kingdom, the most powerful man beneath the heavens!","Now that his daughter had been returned to the imperial family, of course she had to enjoy the finest glory and riches in the world.","What did Noble Consort Jing’s paltry fortune amount to?","If his daughter liked something, what did it matter if he handed her the keys to the imperial treasury?","Su Zhen secretly basked in his own satisfaction, the pride of a father swelling endlessly in his chest.","He felt that the past thirty-some years of his life—spent doing nothing but killing people, reviewing memorials, and suppressing powerful ministers—had all been wasted.","Only today, after hearing his daughter’s inner thoughts, had he experienced the true joy of being emperor.","Wasn’t it all about making money?","The Great Yuan Kingdom might lack many things, but wealthy aristocratic clans and corrupt officials were as numerous as oxen’s hair.","From now on, whoever dared to provoke his precious daughter, he would confiscate their entire household and have all their money hauled to her!","Su Zhen was in an excellent mood, and he couldn’t suppress the smile tugging at his lips.","He glanced at Su Yaoyao, who was still counting her money inside the hall, and decided not to disturb her enjoyment.","The night was already deep. Tomorrow, he still had to attend the morning court and face that troublesome crowd of civil and military officials.","Especially those few censors who prided themselves on being upright scholars and pointed at his nose every day, calling him a tyrant. Just thinking about them gave him a headache.","Su Zhen turned around and lifted his dragon-booted foot, preparing to leave for his own chambers and rest.","However, at the very instant his toes left the ground, Su Yaoyao’s inner voice inside the hall took a sharp one-hundred-and-eighty-degree turn.","【But... even though this money is easy to earn, I can’t keep milking these few sheep in the harem forever, can I?】","【No matter how wealthy the imperial consorts are, their fortunes mostly consist of jewelry and cosmetics. They can’t make me truly rich.】","【If I really want serious money to build my heavy-weapons arsenal, I’ll have to set my sights farther ahead.】","Su Yaoyao sat cross-legged atop a pile of banknotes, stroking her chin. Her little face wore an unusually solemn, thoughtful expression.","【Those high officials in the outer court should have much more money to squeeze out of them.】","【Let me think... Tomorrow is the day of morning court, isn’t it?】","Outside the window, Su Zhen raised an eyebrow.","【What was the name of that old man who points at my dad’s nose and calls him a tyrant every day in court?】","【Oh, right—the Left Censor-in-Chief! The Chief Censor!】","【That old bastard wears patched court robes every day, showing off how incorruptible he is. He claims he’s lived on plain porridge for three years.】","【Whenever my dad spends any money, he threatens to kill himself by smashing his head against a pillar, shouting that Dad is squandering the people’s wealth.】","At this, Su Zhen’s expression darkened.","That’s right. The damn Left Censor-in-Chief!","That old bastard relied on his seniority and reputation as a model for scholars across the realm to make life difficult for him in court.","His reputation for integrity was simply too great. Killing him would easily stir up unrest among scholars throughout the realm, but leaving him alive was infuriating.","Every time Su Zhen went to court and saw that righteous, orange-peel-like old face, he wanted nothing more than to draw his sword and hack it off.","【But...】","Su Yaoyao’s inner voice rose an entire octave.","【That old bastard looks so poor on the surface, presenting himself as a good official devoted to the nation and its people.】","【But in reality, he’s filthy rich—a corrupt official rotten to the bone!】","What?!","Outside the window, Su Zhen’s eyes widened, and his heart shook violently.","The Left Censor-in-Chief? A corrupt official?","Wasn’t the old bastard supposed to be the most incorruptible official in the entire Great Yuan Kingdom?","Even the carriage at his home leaked air!","He was embezzling money? How was that possible?","Su Zhen’s breathing stopped. He pricked up his ears.","Inside the hall, Su Yaoyao snatched up the gold abacus in front of her and slammed it hard against the bed.","【He certainly puts on a convincing act.】","【But I know exactly what color underwear he’s wearing!】","【In the rear courtyard of his home, there’s a dried-up well that’s been abandoned for more than a decade.】","【The mouth of the well is covered by an enormous slab of bluestone, with moss growing all over it. It looks completely innocuous.】","【But who would have thought that at the very bottom of that dried-up well, he had dug out a secret chamber?】","Su Yaoyao grew more excited as she spoke and couldn’t help standing up on the bed.","【There are dozens of huge iron chests stacked inside!】","【They’re filled with all the silver he’s embezzled over the years by abusing his authority, bribing officials above and below him, and lining his own pockets!】","【There’s also the relief silver the imperial court allocated during the Jiangnan floods three years ago!】","【At the bottom of that dried-up well, he’s hidden a full three hundred thousand taels of silver!】","Three hundred thousand taels!!!","The enormous figure exploded in Su Zhen’s mind.","The sheer magnitude of this unexpected windfall nearly blew the top off his skull!","The Great Abyss Kingdom’s entire annual tax revenue amounted to no more than two million taels of silver.","That old bastard had embezzled nearly one-sixth of the national treasury’s yearly income all by himself!","And there was the disaster-relief silver allocated to Jiangnan, too!","The evidence was ironclad. As long as they could dig the silver bearing the official seal out of that dry well, that old bastard’s carefully cultivated reputation as a virtuous, incorruptible official would be torn to shreds!","When that time came, His Majesty could behead the old dog openly and silence the grumbling of the masses.","He could also justifiably and legitimately deposit those three hundred thousand taels of silver into the national treasury!","No!","Into his precious daughter’s private treasury!","Outside the window.","Su Zhen, who had been about to leave, stopped in his tracks.","Su Zhen’s mighty frame shuddered, and his entire aura underwent a earth-shaking transformation.","He turned around and peered through the gaps in the window lattice at the grand canopied bed piled high with gold and silver inside the hall.","In the darkness of night, the emperor’s imposing, fathomless eyes were no longer touched by the slightest trace of sleep.","Instead, they blazed with bloodthirsty greed.","A cruel, eager smile curled up the corners of Su Zhen’s mouth.","His slender fingers tightened around the hilt of the Longquan Sword at his waist, the veins on the back of his hand bulging.","Well, well.","What a windfall!","He had been worrying about having to listen to those civil officials squawk and grumble again at tomorrow’s morning court.","But now, it seemed tomorrow’s court session was going to be very interesting indeed.","Just you wait, old bastard!"]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: In today's morning court, I shall bring her along to attend","paragraphs":["The night wind was cool.","The imperial palace of Great Yuan was roiling with hidden currents.","Su Zhen had just returned to the Imperial Study from outside Zhaoyang Hall, striding so quickly that sparks seemed to fly from his feet.","He had not even taken an imperial carriage. He walked with such force that a gust of wind followed in his wake.","The eunuchs behind him had to jog the entire way, panting and utterly bewildered.","When His Majesty had gone to Zhaoyang Hall, he had been brimming with murderous intent, looking as though he meant to swallow Noble Consort Jing alive.","So how had he returned with a face still stern, yet steps so light and buoyant? He looked like a several-hundred-pound child in a fit of happiness.","With a resounding bang, Su Zhen kicked open the heavy, carved wooden doors of the Imperial Study.","“Every one of you, get out! Without My permission, no one is to come within fifty paces of the Imperial Study!”","The eunuchs fled as though they had been granted a pardon, scrambling out on all fours.","Soon, only Su Zhen remained inside the Imperial Study.","He could no longer contain the joy surging through his heart. He paced back and forth across the spacious room.","Three hundred thousand taels!","That was a full three hundred thousand taels of silver!","Great Yuan had been short of money everywhere these past few years. The treasury was so impoverished that even a rat would have to leave with tears in its eyes after entering.","The soldiers guarding the borders needed provisions and pay. Disaster relief funds had to be sent to every corner of the realm. Which of those things did not require silver?","As Emperor, he could not even repair a garden without being roundly condemned by the censors for squandering the people’s labor and wealth.","And yet—","The very man who cursed him day after day, proclaiming himself Great Yuan’s Foremost Incorruptible Official, had hidden a fortune of three hundred thousand taels beneath a withered well in his own backyard!","“You old bastard! No wonder you never lose weight, even though you drink nothing but thin gruel every day. So all that grease has been going straight into your belly!”","Su Zhen slapped the red sandalwood desk, his eyes gleaming like a hungry wolf’s.","He took a deep breath and forced himself to calm down before shouting in a low voice, “Shadow!”","As soon as the words left his mouth, the air in a corner of the Imperial Study twisted.","A commander of the imperial secret guard, dressed entirely in black, appeared before Su Zhen like a specter and dropped to one knee.","“Your subordinate is here!”","Shadow’s voice was as cold and hard as iron.","As the most mysterious and lethal imperial secret guard in Great Yuan, Shadow answered only to the Emperor.","The Emperor summoned them only when investigating a major treason case or assassinating an important official of an enemy state.","Shadow had already prepared himself for orders to slaughter an entire powerful minister’s household.","“Immediately gather the most elite Heaven-grade secret guards under your command and leave the palace.”","Su Zhen lowered his voice, his tone ruthless.","Shadow’s spirits lifted. He tightened his grip on the hilt at his waist.","“Your Majesty, which residence are we to purge tonight?”","“Not purge. I want you to keep watch.”","Su Zhen walked up to Shadow and issued his order slowly, one word at a time.","“Go to the residence of the Left Censor-in-Chief.”","“Surround that abandoned withered well in his backyard—the one covered by a slab of blue stone—and guard it with your lives!”","Shadow froze. Shock flashed through his eyes beneath his mask.","Keep watch... over a withered well?","Deploy the most elite assassins of the Heaven grade to watch a withered well in some old man’s backyard?","“Your Majesty, is there perhaps some weapon or group of hidden soldiers plotting rebellion concealed in that well?” Shadow could not help asking.","“It is more important than weapons!”","Su Zhen let out a cold laugh.","“That well contains My imperial treasury!”","Shadow’s heart jolted.","Although he could not understand the riddle, he did not dare ask any further questions.","“Convey My absolute order!” Su Zhen’s gaze turned incomparably cold, like an abyss.","“From this moment until the end of tomorrow’s court session, not even a fly is to leave the area around that withered well!”","“If so much as one brick goes missing from the well, or if anyone approaches it, I will exterminate your entire clans!”","Shadow trembled from head to toe and cupped his fists.","“Your subordinate obeys! We swear to defend the well with our lives!”","The night wind swept past, and Shadow’s figure vanished.","Su Zhen braced both hands against his desk and gazed into the darkness outside the window. No matter how hard he tried, he could not suppress the smile tugging at his lips.","Everything was ready. All that remained was for the east wind to blow.","Tomorrow’s court session would certainly be a magnificent spectacle.","—","The residence of the Left Censor-in-Chief, east of the capital.","From the outside, the house looked decrepit. The plaster had fallen from the walls, and the red paint on the main gate had peeled away in mottled patches.","It was even shabbier than the homes of the capital’s most down-and-out merchants.","This was precisely what the Left Censor-in-Chief took the greatest pride in. He used the dilapidated residence as a living emblem of his own uprightness and incorruptibility.","Whenever a colleague came to visit and saw the run-down gate, they would be moved to tears.","Yet deep within the residence, in a secret study, an entirely different scene unfolded.","The Left Censor-in-Chief sat behind a fine huanghuali wood desk.","A Donghai mermaid candle worth a thousand pieces of gold burned on the table, releasing a faint fragrance and illuminating the entire study as brightly as daylight.","He wore his trademark court robe, patched in three places.","But the robe’s lining was made of Jiangnan Cloudflow Silk, worth a thousand pieces of gold per bolt. It kept him warm in winter and cool in summer against his skin.","The Left Censor-in-Chief lifted a purple-clay teapot and leisurely took a sip of Wuyi Da Hong Pao, rushed to him by an express courier from a thousand li away.","He set down the teapot, picked up a white-jade wolf-hair brush, and began writing furiously on the memorial before him.","His expression shifted between deep anguish and righteous indignation.","His words flowed in grand, magnificent prose, as though he alone in all the world remained clearheaded and loyal.","Every line of the memorial was cutting enough to draw blood.","He was impeaching the Emperor for being bewitched by a Demoness, bringing the Bastard from the Black Market into the palace, and even conferring upon her the title of Crown Princess.","For the sake of that bastard, the Emperor had unjustly punished Noble Consort Jing, who assisted in managing the six palaces. Such conduct was that of a Tyrant.","“The Demoness has thrown the government into chaos, and the realm is on the verge of ruin! If Your Majesty remains stubborn and refuses to see reason, this old minister can only die to atone before all under Heaven!”","After writing the final sentence, the Left Censor-in-Chief brought the brush down heavily and tapped it against the inkstone.","He looked at the impeaching memorial, a masterpiece destined to last through the ages, and stroked his graying beard in satisfaction.","He could already imagine the magnificent scene at tomorrow’s court session.","Before all the civil and military officials, he would denounce the Tyrant with righteous indignation and condemn the Crown Princess of unknown origins.","When the Tyrant flew into a rage, he would pretend to dash his head against the coiled-dragon pillar in the Golden Hall, staging a death remonstrance.","Of course, it would only be an act.","He had practiced the angle at home countless times. At most, he would suffer a little scrape.","But once he made that single charge, his title as Great Yuan’s Foremost Upright Courtier would be recorded in the annals of history.","The scholars of the realm would revere him as a saint, and under the pressure of public opinion, the Tyrant would have no choice but to obediently compromise.","As for the dozen or so tens of thousands of taels his wastrel son had lost at the underground gambling den during the day...","The Left Censor-in-Chief gave a cold laugh, greed flashing in his eyes.","As long as his reputation remained intact and he retained his power, the silver could always be extorted back—multiplied several times over.","He carefully tucked the memorial into his sleeve.","At that moment, he was immersed in a beautiful dream of having his name remembered for all time and wielding power over the entire court.","The night slowly faded, and the eastern sky began to pale.","Dawn broke. Another morning had arrived.","Inside the Panlong Hall of Great Yuan’s imperial palace—","As was customary, at this hour the Emperor would still be asleep. No one dared disturb the Tyrant’s fearsome temper upon waking.","But today, everything was different.","For the first time ever, Su Zhen had risen a full hour earlier than usual.","The eunuchs and palace maids waiting outside the hall trembled as they carried in the bronze basins and warm water for his morning ablutions.","Had His Majesty risen so early because he had slept poorly the night before and was seething with anger, ready to begin another massacre?","The newly appointed chief eunuch pushed open the door with great trepidation.","Su Zhen was already fully dressed. He stood before the enormous bronze mirror, looking invigorated, his eyes shining brightly.","There was not the slightest trace of his usual morning temper.","He could hardly contain his excitement, as if he were about to attend a grand celebration!","“Move faster! What are you dawdling for?”","Su Zhen impatiently urged the eunuchs, who were still standing there in a daze.","“If you delay My morning court session or interfere with My important affairs, I’ll have your heads cut off!”","The eunuchs hurried forward in terror to help the emperor fasten his jade-inlaid belt and arrange his ornaments.","Su Zhen ran his hand over the jade-inlaid sword at his waist, a smile full of anticipation curling at the corners of his lips.","His fingers tapped lightly against the hilt, producing a chilling sound.","“You old bastard, I’m taking your three hundred thousand taels today, no matter what.”","Su Zhen muttered under his breath, sending a shiver down anyone who heard him.","Dong.","Dong.","The Jingyang Bell suddenly rang out above the imperial city.","Its deep, resonant tolls pierced the thin chill of the morning mist, announcing the beginning of a new day.","Outside the Meridian Gate, civil and military officials dressed in immaculate court robes entered in an orderly procession, treading over the morning dew.","Each wore a different expression.","The Left Censor-in-Chief held his head high and puffed out his chest, looking as though he were ready to make a great show of himself.","Outside the Hall of Golden Chimes, the atmosphere was solemn and grave.","Su Zhen stood behind the gilded screen at the rear of the great hall, listening to the sounds of the assembled officials paying their respects outside.","He turned his head toward the chief eunuch standing respectfully beside him.","A wicked glint flashed through the Tyrant’s eyes.","He said to the chief eunuch, “Go. Bring the Crown Princess here. I’m taking her to court with Me today!”"]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: An old minister has been poor all his life, serving as an official for thirty years, with clean hands and no corruption","paragraphs":["The Golden Hall of the Great Abyss Kingdom’s imperial palace.","This magnificent palace, which symbolized the highest imperial authority under heaven, was filled with an unusually solemn and grave atmosphere.","The civil and military officials stood in orderly rows inside the great hall, dressed in immaculate court robes and arranged according to rank.","Every face was tense, as though a storm were about to break.","The commotion at the Zhaoyang Hall and the Chuxiu Palace the previous night had been far too great to escape the notice of these court officials with their countless sources of information.","The dignified Noble Consort Jing, head of the imperial harem, had actually been placed under house arrest by an eight-year-old country girl who had only just been brought back to the palace. Even her entire fortune had been thoroughly confiscated!","What was the kingdom coming to?","If this Crown Princess of unknown origins were allowed to continue running wild, wouldn’t the entire court of the Great Abyss Kingdom descend into chaos?","At the very front of the civil officials stood an old man with a full head of white hair and a face brimming with righteous indignation.","He was none other than the Left Censor-in-Chief, head of the kingdom’s censors.","His court robe had been washed until it had faded, and several patches could be seen on it.","He stood perfectly straight, like an unshakable pillar holding up the sea and heavens. From head to toe, he radiated the noble brilliance of honesty and incorruptibility.","The Left Censor-in-Chief narrowed his eyes as he silently reviewed the contents of the impeachment memorial hidden in his sleeve.","Today, he would not only impeach that little demon. He would also use this opportunity to properly admonish the increasingly tyrannical emperor.","He had already decided exactly how loud his voice should be and how sorrowful his expression should look, so that he could display the bearing of a loyal minister before the entire court.","His name would go down in history.","Today was the day!","“His Majesty the Emperor has arrived—!”","The chief eunuch’s shrill, piercing announcement rang through the hall.","The Golden Hall fell so silent that one could hear a pin drop.","“We pay our respects to Your Majesty! Long live Your Majesty! Long live Your Majesty! Long, long live Your Majesty!”","The civil and military officials dropped to their knees in unison and shouted their greetings.","Steady, powerful footsteps came from behind the screen at the rear of the hall.","Su Zhen strode forward in a majestic black-and-gold robe embroidered with nine dragons and walked up the white jade steps.","However, after the officials had finished paying their respects, they cautiously raised their heads, preparing to hear the emperor’s instructions.","The entire Golden Hall sank into an eerie silence.","Everyone’s eyes widened.","Several elderly ministers rubbed their eyes in disbelief, wondering if their advanced age had finally caused them to see things.","Because the ruthless and cold-blooded tyrant, Su Zhen—","was not walking up to the dragon throne empty-handed.","In his arms, he was carrying a small pink quilt made of priceless Shu brocade, bundled into a neat roll!","A round little face, flushed from sleep and chubby with baby fat, poked out from inside.","The newly appointed Crown Princess of the Great Abyss Kingdom, Su Yaoyao, was sleeping soundly in her Tyrant Dad’s arms!","A glistening bead of drool hung from the corner of her mouth. With every breath, it formed and popped into a tiny bubble.","The worldview of every civil and military official in the hall shattered into dust.","This was the Golden Hall!","The sacred court where the Great Abyss Kingdom discussed important matters of state and military affairs!","His Majesty had actually carried a little girl who was still sleeping in late to the morning court?!","What had become of the Great Abyss Kingdom’s century-old court traditions?!","The Left Censor-in-Chief trembled with rage, his white beard quivering violently in midair.","Absurd!","The height of ridiculousness!","He was just about to step out of formation and begin his grand impeachment—","when several eunuchs serving before the emperor emerged from behind the hall, carefully carrying a chair.","It was a specially made miniature throne.","The entire chair was crafted from pure gold, and its back was encrusted with so many diamonds and rubies and sapphires that they nearly blinded the eye.","Under the bright candlelight of the Golden Hall, the little golden throne radiated an impossible-to-ignore aura of nouveau riche extravagance.","The eunuchs cautiously placed the diamond-studded golden seat beside the dragon throne, which represented the highest power under heaven.","It was only half a step away!","Holding Su Yaoyao, Su Zhen bent down slowly, his movements as gentle as though he were handling a priceless treasure. He carefully settled his daughter, still wrapped in her little quilt, onto the diamond-studded golden seat.","Then he thoughtfully tucked the quilt around her.","“Phew...”","The movement disturbed Su Yaoyao.","She smacked her lips sleepily, then slowly opened her limpid, peach-blossom eyes.","She raised her short, chubby hands and rubbed her eyes. Then, right in front of the entire court, she opened her mouth and let out a tremendous yawn.","“Yaaawn... I’m so sleepy...”","Su Yaoyao complained furiously inside her head.","[What is this nonsense?! It’s not even dawn yet, and the roosters haven’t even crowed! Why did they drag me out of bed?!]","[Lining up for morning court in ancient times is even more inhumane than mining coal on a resource star in the interstellar age!]","[Lack of sleep is going to affect the development of this eight-year-old body, okay?!]","Hearing his daughter’s aggrieved complaints, a trace of indulgent amusement flashed through Su Zhen’s eyes as he sat on the dragon throne.","If not for today’s grand confiscation spectacle, he would never have had the heart to wake his precious daughter so early.","After finishing her yawn, Su Yaoyao looked around in confusion.","When she saw the mass of old men kneeling below her in court robes of various colors, she finally became somewhat more alert.","[Oh, right. I’m here to watch the show from the front row.]","[How can I watch a show without snacks?]","Su Yaoyao fumbled around inside her quilt. Under its cover, her consciousness connected with her portable interstellar storage space.","The next second—","under the horrified, unbelieving gazes of the entire court, the Crown Princess pulled half a golden-brown, sizzling roast leg of lamb out of her pink quilt!","It was the leftover snack she had eaten while staying up late to draw blueprints the previous night, then placed in the storage space’s preservation cabinet.","Now, it was still at the perfect temperature.","Su Yaoyao held the half leg of lamb, which was even larger than her face, in both hands.","She opened her mouth and took a huge bite, tearing off a large chunk of crisp, roasted meat.","“Chomp, chomp, chomp...”","Her cheeks bulging as she chewed, she swung her little legs back and forth above the floor.","The rich fragrance of cumin and chili powder mingled with the overpowering aroma of lamb fat roasting over a fire.","It swept through the solemn Golden Hall like a tornado.","The sound of countless people swallowing nervously mingled with sharp intakes of breath.","On one side were the trembling officials, who scarcely dared to breathe.","On the other was the Crown Princess, sitting on her diamond-studded golden chair, her mouth slick with grease as she devoured roast meat.","Was this still a court session?","The Left Censor-in-Chief could no longer tolerate such unbearable humiliation.","The Great Abyss Kingdom’s century-old dignity was being destroyed one mouthful of cumin-seasoned lamb at a time!","“Your Majesty!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief stepped out of formation, his voice shrill and tragic, like a cuckoo crying blood.","With a trembling finger, he pointed straight at Su Yaoyao, who was gnawing on a leg of lamb beside the dragon throne.","“You little demon! You have thrown the imperial harem into chaos, and now you dare come to this sacred court and run wild!”","“Above us are the hundred years of the Great Abyss Kingdom’s court traditions, and the spirits of our imperial ancestors!”","“How can we allow a mere child to sit here wrapped in a quilt, gnawing on a leg of lamb while listening in on affairs of state?!”","The more the Left Censor-in-Chief spoke, the more agitated he became. His eyes reddened as though he had suffered some terrible injustice.","“If Your Majesty does not immediately strip this little demon of her position as Crown Princess and drive her out of the hall—”","“then this old minister will die right here in the Golden Hall today, to prove his convictions!”","His words rang out with force, filled with righteousness and moral indignation.","Several other civil officials also stepped forward and fell to their knees, shouting, “Your Majesty, please think twice! Abolish the Crown Princess!”","The atmosphere was taut, ready to explode.","Everyone assumed that in the face of the chief censor’s remonstrance unto death, even a tyrant as biased as the emperor would have to show some consideration for public opinion.","Yet Su Zhen merely leaned coldly against the imperial throne. Turning his head, he took a snow-white handkerchief from the eunuch and gently wiped the cumin powder from the corner of Su Yaoyao’s mouth as she watched the spectacle.","“Slow down. Don’t choke. The roast mutton is a little tough. Tomorrow, I’ll have the Imperial Kitchen roast you a tender suckling pig.”","Su Zhen’s voice was so gentle it seemed sweet enough to melt, completely treating the Left Censor-in-Chief’s hoarse cries below as though they were nothing but air.","Su Yaoyao bit into her mutton and blinked innocently with her clear, wide eyes.","【Tsk, tsk, tsk. That old man has some impressive lung capacity. What a shame he didn’t become a tenor.】","【So this is the corrupt official who has three hundred thousand taels of embezzled silver hidden at home? His acting is incredible.】","Seeing that the tyrant was completely ignoring him and was instead putting on a touching display of fatherly affection with that bastard, the Left Censor-in-Chief felt his fury and humiliation surge to their peak.","So he wasn’t going to give him any face, was he?","Fine!","Then he would make a huge scene today and see who ended up unable to save face!","“Corrupt emperor! Demon child!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief rose to his feet, hair disheveled, and cried out toward the heavens in grief and indignation.","“I have lived in poverty my entire life! I have served as an official for thirty years and remained incorruptible!”","“For the sake of Dayuan’s state and people, I eat nothing but plain porridge and simple vegetables at every meal. I cannot even bring myself to have a decent court robe made!”","“Now that the imperial court has fallen into chaos, what meaning is there in my continuing to live?”","He closed his eyes, his face taking on the resolute expression of a man prepared to die.","“I have no choice but to remonstrate with my life, in repayment for the late emperor’s kindness in recognizing my worth!”","With that, the Left Censor-in-Chief turned around.","Head lowered and eyes shut, he charged toward the thickest coiled-dragon pillar in the Golden Hall like a mad old bull!"]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: That Is My Money","paragraphs":["His strides were enormous, his wide sleeves billowing as he charged forward with the unstoppable force of a tiger descending the mountain.","In reality, however, his murky old eyes were peering through the slits of his eyelids, carefully measuring the distance between himself and the coiled-dragon pillar.","Even the rhythm of his steps concealed a trick. There was plenty of thunder, but hardly any rain—the speed of his charge was nowhere near enough to prove fatal.","“Your Excellency, you mustn’t!”","“Lord Left Censor-in-Chief, think this through! The Great Abyss Kingdom cannot afford to lose you!”","The upright scholar-officials behind him, completely unaware of what was really going on, shed tears of emotion one after another. Their wails rang through the entire hall.","Several young officials had rehearsed this scene with him countless times, and their coordination was flawless.","They rushed forward like hungry tigers pouncing on prey, wrapped their arms around the Left Censor-in-Chief’s waist, and clung tightly to his legs.","“My lord! Please stop!”","“If you throw your life away, how can Heaven’s justice endure?!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief struggled violently, shouting in grief and outrage, “Let go of this old man! Let me die!”","His movements were enormous, but he did not move forward even a single inch.","The Golden Chime Palace had become the perfect stage for these upright scholar-officials to show off their acting skills.","They wailed and cried to the heavens, putting on a magnificent performance of a loyal minister suffering for his principles.","From the Dragon Throne, the tyrant Su Zhen watched the hypocritical farce below with icy indifference.","His eyes churned with bone-chilling killing intent.","These old bastards who prided themselves on their moral purity relied on the opinions of scholars across the realm to play this game of moral coercion in court every single day.","Did they really think the Longquan Sword in his hand was dull?","Since you want to die so badly, then I’ll grant your wish today!","Su Zhen’s hand moved toward the hilt at his waist, his knuckles tightening.","He was just about to give the order for the Imperial Guards to chop off the old bastard’s head and hang it outside the Meridian Gate for public display.","At that critical moment...","A remarkably crisp sound came from the little chair beside him, a chair made of pure gold and studded with diamonds.","“Tsk, tsk, tsk...”","The sound was not loud, but amid the wailing of the assembled officials, it was particularly jarring.","Su Zhen’s hand froze on the sword hilt.","He turned his head and looked at his precious daughter, who was sitting beside him and enthusiastically devouring a roasted leg of lamb.","Su Yaoyao’s eyes were shining as she held up half a roasted leg, golden-brown and glistening with oil.","She chewed the meat while watching the officials below, who were crying themselves into a heap, with great interest.","Her clear eyes glittered with the mocking amusement of someone who had seen through the ways of the world—as though she were watching a traveling troupe perform acrobatics.","[This old geezer’s acting is incredible! The Oscars owe him a little golden statuette!]","[Those fake moves, that positioning, those exaggerated microexpressions—what a loss to the Great Abyss Kingdom’s opera houses that he never took the stage!]","Su Yaoyao unleashed her complaints in her head, and her thoughts exploded through Su Zhen’s mind like a rapid-fire cannon.","[And he’s always shouting about living on plain porridge and simple vegetables? Claiming he’s spent his whole life poor and devoted to the people?]","[I’m embarrassed for that orange-peel face of his!]","[Every night, after everyone in his household has fallen asleep, the old man sneaks into the secret passage in the rear courtyard like a thief.]","[The cellar is lit by roaring charcoal fires, and a master chef hired at great expense from Lingnan has long since prepared a suckling pig that was barely a month old, its skin crisp and its meat tender.]","[He bites into it with a loud crunch, grease running down the corners of his mouth. The way he eats is more savage than a starving wolf.]","[That charcoal-roasted suckling pig, crisp on the outside, tender within, and sizzling with fat—he can polish off more than half of one by himself in a single meal!]","From the Dragon Throne, the corner of Su Zhen’s mouth twitched violently.","Charcoal-roasted suckling pig? Sneaking food at midnight?","So this was the Left Censor-in-Chief, supposedly so pure and incorruptible that he lived on nothing but plain porridge and vegetables!","Su Yaoyao’s thoughts were filled with scorn.","[After stuffing himself full, he even uses the finest scented mouthwash to rinse his mouth, terrified that someone will smell the meat on his breath when he attends court the next day.]","[He eats rich, greasy food like this every day and has managed to give himself high blood pressure, high blood lipids, and high blood sugar!]","[It’s only because this ancient era doesn’t have medical testing equipment. Otherwise, his three-high numbers would scare the Imperial Medical Academy’s chief physician to death on the spot!]","Although Su Zhen had no idea what “the three highs” or “the Oscars” meant, he understood perfectly well that the old bastard gorged himself on delicacies every night in a cellar.","And yet just now, he had put on an emaciated look, as though he were about to collapse from hunger at any moment!","Su Zhen forcibly suppressed the urge to laugh. Without revealing anything, he shifted a little closer to Su Yaoyao.","[And that ragged court robe he’s wearing is a miracle of ancient haute couture!]","Su Yaoyao took a huge bite of lamb and continued ruthlessly exposing the old man’s secrets in her mind.","[He wears patched clothes to court every day, claiming he’s so poor he can’t even afford to have a new outfit made.]","[And this bunch of ignorant bookworms actually believes him!]","[That robe cost him a thousand taels of silver. He went all the way to Jiangnan and hired the finest embroiderer to make that “ragged” outfit to his exact measurements!]","A thousand taels?!","Su Zhen sucked in a sharp breath.","The official salary openly paid to a first-rank official of the Great Abyss Kingdom amounted to little more than two hundred taels of silver a year.","Yet a single “ragged” court robe of his had cost a thousand taels?!","[The fabric looks coarse, but it’s actually rare old homespun from Jiangnan—warm in winter, cool in summer, and exceptionally breathable.]","[To make the robe look worn, the embroiderer soaked it in a special herbal solution for forty-nine days.]","[Even the positions of the patches were calculated by a feng shui master. It was all about the beauty of imperfection.]","Su Yaoyao swallowed the meat in her mouth and took a sip of tea to cut through the grease, thoroughly delighted.","[And inside the lining beneath those patches, there are countless threads woven and sewn from pure gold!]","[When the wind blows, the gold threads glimmer faintly in the sunlight. He tells everyone that the shine is just the result of washing the clothes until they’ve faded.]","[The gold thread hidden inside that robe alone would be enough to feed an ordinary family for an entire lifetime!]","[A thousand taels of silver for a single ragged robe, and he still has the nerve to cry poverty and perform a deathbed remonstration here? He’s so hypocritical it makes me sick!]","On the Dragon Throne, Su Zhen’s eyes glowed green, like a starving wolf in the dead of night.","Excellent!","Simply excellent!","So this was the “upright scholar” of the Great Abyss Kingdom who cursed him every day in court for extravagance and accused him of caring nothing for the people’s lives?","So this was the moral paragon whom scholars across the realm worshipped?","Su Zhen was so furious that he nearly burst out laughing right there.","He stared coldly at the Left Censor-in-Chief, who was still performing his deathbed remonstrance below, his eyes filled with mockery.","He wanted to see just how long the old bastard could keep up the act.","Su Yaoyao raised the leg of lamb and viciously tore off the last succulent piece of meat.","She chewed loudly before dropping the final bombshell.","[Still, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍considering how desperately the old geezer is performing today, he was probably driven into a corner.]","[He must be panicking like crazy right now, desperate to regain some sense of relevance in court.]","[After all, something major happened to the huge sum of money he hid in his ancestral grave last night.]","As soon as these thoughts emerged, Su Zhen’s ears pricked up.","His imperial eyes shone a hundred times brighter than lightbulbs.","His ancestral grave? A huge sum of money?!","The thirty thousand taels hidden in the dry well outside Zhaoyang Hall, which he had learned about while eavesdropping outside the window the previous night, had already left him too excited to sleep.","And now there was an even greater surprise hidden in the old man’s ancestral grave?!","Su Yaoyao wiped the grease from the corner of her mouth.","[The old geezer went to great lengths to hide five hundred thousand taels of embezzled money in his family’s ancestral grave.]","[He thought no one would ever find out. He even used his own ancestor’s coffin as a shield.]","【You can guard against outsiders day and night, but you can never guard against a thief in your own house!】","Five hundred thousand taels?!","Su Zhen felt as though the enormous figure had nearly blown the top off his skull.","【Last night, his wastrel son—equally skilled at eating, drinking, whoring, and gambling—owed a huge gambling debt to an underground casino.】","【The scoundrel had actually brought a group of men in the middle of the night to dig up his own family’s ancestral tomb!】","【A full five hundred thousand taels of silver—his son had hauled it all to the casino overnight and lost more than half of it in a single night!】","【If the old man found out, he probably wouldn’t even need to pretend to bang his head against a pillar. He’d be so furious he’d suffer a cerebral hemorrhage and drop dead on the spot!】","Five hundred thousand taels! An ancestral tomb! A wastrel son! Half lost at an underground casino!","This explosive stream of information struck Su Zhen’s forehead like nine bolts of heavenly thunder.","Three hundred thousand taels plus five hundred thousand taels—that made a full eight hundred thousand taels of silver!","That old bastard alone was worth half the treasury of the Great Abyss Kingdom!","And now, half of it had actually been lost at a casino by some worthless wastrel?!","That was His Majesty’s money!!!","Uncontrollable fury and elation shattered Su Zhen’s reason.","“Bang!”","A deafening crash rang out.","Su Zhen slammed his palm onto the imperial desk. His tall, imposing body rose abruptly, like a frenzied dragon awakening!"]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: Go dig up my beloved minister's ancestral grave...","paragraphs":["The force with which Su Zhen slammed his fist onto the dragon-carved imperial desk was so tremendous that even the solid-gold paperweight bounced half a foot into the air before rolling clatteringly down the white-jade steps.","The civil and military officials in the hall, who had been fake-crying and wailing moments ago, were so startled by the sudden crash that their entire bodies shuddered, their cries catching in their throats.","The several eunuchs standing nearby to guard the Emperor were scared half to death.","Thinking an assassin had startled the Emperor, they hurriedly spread their arms and tried to shield him with their bodies.","“Get out of the way—all of you!”","Su Zhen’s furious roar was like the bellow of a ferocious tiger.","Without the slightest mercy, he shoved aside the eunuchs and guards blocking his path. His tall, straight figure sent a sharp gust of wind through the air as he charged down the white-jade steps.","He crossed three steps in a single stride. His black-and-gold dragon robe billowed in midair, his imposing presence terrifying.","At the very center of the hall—","The Left Censor-in-Chief had his eyes tightly shut. Striding forward like a maddened old ox, he was charging headfirst at the thickest coiled-dragon pillar.","He calculated the distance excitedly in his mind.","Three steps left!","Two!","He was about to hit it!","As long as his forehead merely scraped off a layer of skin and squeezed out a few drops of blood, his immortal reputation as Great Yuan’s Foremost Upright Courtier would be recorded in the annals of history!","The corners of the Left Censor-in-Chief’s mouth rose involuntarily.","Just as his forehead was only an inch away from the hard pillar, an immense force suddenly surged from the back of his neck, vast and overwhelming.","The Left Censor-in-Chief felt his neck tighten, cutting off his breath.","His charging body came to an abrupt halt in midair, as though seized by an invisible claw.","“Ow!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief let out a strange cry, both feet leaving the ground.","Su Zhen had grabbed the patched collar of his official robe with one hand and lifted him into the air like a scrawny old rooster.","The Left Censor-in-Chief opened his eyes in terror, his four limbs kicking uselessly in midair.","What filled his vision was Su Zhen’s handsome face, so close that it appeared magnified countless times.","Contrary to everyone’s expectations, Su Zhen’s face was not blazing with fury, nor did it hold the murderous ferocity they had anticipated.","Instead, the Tyrant’s eyes gleamed with an almost fatherly compassion and a bizarre expression of deep heartache.","“My dear minister! My Left Censor-in-Chief!”","Su Zhen raised his voice, every word overflowing with sincere concern and affection.","That single cry left all the civil and military officials utterly dumbfounded.","Even Su Yaoyao, seated on her little golden chair and gnawing on a lamb leg, paused mid-chew and widened her limpid, peach-blossom eyes.","“My dear minister has lived a life of poverty and devoted himself to the country and its people. You are truly a role model for every official in Great Yuan!”","With one hand still holding the Left Censor-in-Chief aloft, Su Zhen used the other to stroke the large patch on his official robe with profound pain.","“Look at this! Just look at it!”","“A dignified first-rank official, yet you cannot even afford a decent official robe. Seeing this patch, the pain in my heart is unbearable!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief was being choked so badly that his eyes rolled back. He could barely breathe.","He had no idea what madness had seized the Tyrant this time. All he could do was desperately wave his hands, trying to pry apart Su Zhen’s ironlike fingers.","“That is why I absolutely cannot stand by and watch a loyal subject like you smash your head against a pillar and die!”","Su Zhen released his grip.","With a wet smack, the Left Censor-in-Chief hit the golden-brick floor like a heap of mud, landing so hard that he was dazed and disoriented.","Before he could even crawl up and offer his thanks, Su Zhen turned around. His majestic gaze swept toward the Imperial Guards outside the hall.","“Guards!”","A squad of heavily armored Imperial Guards strode into the hall and dropped to one knee.","“Your orders, Your Majesty!”","“The Left Censor-in-Chief has lived an incorruptible life. His family cannot even afford to hire a servant to guard their home.”","The corners of Su Zhen’s mouth curled into a demonic smile, his voice booming throughout the Golden Hall.","“I am truly worried about the safety of my dear minister’s ancestral graves!”","“Immediately muster five hundred elite soldiers. Leave the city and go dig up my dear minister’s ancestral tombs—”","Every official in the hall drew a sharp breath, their eyes nearly bulging from their sockets.","Dig up his ancestral tombs?!","“Ahem. I was overcome with grief and misspoke.”","Su Zhen corrected himself without the slightest hint of sincerity, his gaze cold as a blade.","“I meant go protect them! Go and protect my dear minister’s ancestral graves properly!”","“If even one or two silver pieces are missing from those graves, I will hold every one of you accountable!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief, sprawled on the floor, heard the words “ancestral graves” and “silver.” A thunderous boom exploded in his mind.","The blood in his entire body seemed to freeze, and his face turned paler than paper.","How could the Tyrant know about the graves?!","Su Zhen continued unleashing one devastating blow after another.","Looking down at the Left Censor-in-Chief, who was trembling like a sieve, he made his tone even more concerned.","“Oh, that reminds me. There is one more matter.”","“I hear that your only son has recently picked up some unsavory habits and has been staying out all night.”","“You will also go to the underground Bliss Casino in the western part of the city.”","“Bring back that precious son of yours, who is currently slaughtering everyone at the tables, and be sure to ‘invite’ him politely!”","“And while you are there, take inventory of exactly how much hard silver he lost last night!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief’s final psychological defense collapsed completely.","It was as though a heavenly thunderbolt had struck him head-on. His knees went weak, and his entire body slumped to the floor like a pile of mud.","It was over.","It was all over.","The Tyrant knew about the five hundred thousand taels hidden in the ancestral graves and the three hundred thousand taels concealed beneath the dry well!","“Your Majesty, you must not! Your Majesty, have mercy!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief could no longer concern himself with the dignity of an upright official. He scrambled toward Su Zhen on all fours.","Tears and mucus covered his face as he desperately kowtowed against the golden bricks, each impact producing a dull thud.","“This old minister has been wronged! I have lived a life of poverty and honesty. How could I possibly have money to gamble?!”","“These are all slanderous accusations by malicious villains! It was that Demoness who bewitched Your Majesty and filled your ears with lies!”","Even at this point, he still tried to bite back, struggling desperately to survive.","Several censorial officials who usually followed at the Left Censor-in-Chief’s heels also knelt down courageously.","“Your Majesty, please judge the matter wisely! Everyone under heaven knows of the Left Censor-in-Chief’s incorruptibility!”","“How could he possibly have hidden money in his ancestral graves? This is utter nonsense!”","Su Zhen looked at this group of stubborn old hypocrites, the mocking expression in his eyes growing even deeper.","“Incorruptible? Utter nonsense?”","Su Zhen let out a cold laugh.","The sound seemed to come from the depths of the netherworld, sending chills down everyone’s spines.","He had no patience left to argue with this pack of false gentlemen. Taking a step back, he shouted sharply:","“Where are the saber guards?”","Two burly saber guards with faces cold as iron strode forward.","“Strip him bare!”","“Let the entire court see with their own eyes just how poor our Great Yuan’s Foremost Incorruptible Official truly is!”","The two guards accepted the order and lunged at the Left Censor-in-Chief.","One on each side, they pinned down his wildly struggling arms.","“Let go of this old man! What are you doing?! This is an insult to scholarship! An insult to scholarship!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief screamed shrilly, like an old dog driven into a desperate corner.","But the guards’ strength was immense, leaving him no room to resist.","One of them seized the faded patch over the chest of his official robe.","Then he pulled hard!","Riiip!","The sound of tearing fabric rang through the hall.","The tattered official robe, which he claimed to have worn for ten years and mended countless times, was brutally ripped open from the collar all the way down to the waist.","The newly risen morning sun happened to shine through the carved lattice windows outside the hall, casting its slanting rays inside.","The sunlight fell upon the lining beneath the Left Censor-in-Chief’s torn robe.","A dazzling, eye-searing golden radiance suddenly burst forth!","The entire hall drew a collective, perfectly synchronized gasp.","The inside of the coarse court robe was actually lined with Jiangnan Flowing-Cloud Brocade—the most expensive and softest fabric in the entire realm.","Beneath the patches, densely packed and crisscrossing one another, were threads made entirely of pure gold!","The golden threads formed intricate, magnificent patterns, glittering brilliantly beneath the sunlight. The sheer extravagance was breathtaking.","A tattered robe?","It was clearly a one-of-a-kind golden battle armor hidden beneath a ragged outer garment!","Inside the Golden Hall, an utter silence descended.","The few censorial officials who had just pleaded for him looked like ducks being strangled. Their mouths hung open, but not a sound came out.","They stared wide-eyed at the dazzling golden light, their entire world collapsing around them.","Was this the moral paragon they had revered as a deity?","Was this the leader who lectured them every day about purging their desires and worrying for the nation and its people?","The cost of a single undergarment was worth ten years of an ordinary official’s salary!","The Left Censor-in-Chief collapsed onto the floor, staring at the golden-thread lining now exposed to the air. He stopped struggling.","His eyes were vacant, his lips blue. In an instant, he seemed ten years older, reduced to nothing more than a soulless shell.","“So much for a lifetime of poverty! So much for eating nothing but plain porridge and simple side dishes at every meal!”","Su Zhen’s voice exploded through the hall like a thunderclap, ringing in every person’s ears.","“You old scoundrel—deceiving the world and stealing its reputation while embezzling public funds and violating the law!”","The Left Censor-in-Chief collapsed like a puddle of mud, fainting on the floor as he wheezed like a dying dog.","Once again, a suffocating silence filled the great hall.","Not a single person dared to speak. Even their breathing was deliberately restrained, lest they provoke the Tyrant’s wrath.","Time passed, second by second.","Su Zhen did not announce the end of court. He merely sat quietly upon the throne, his fingers lightly tapping against the desk.","Half an hour later—","A series of heavy, hurried footsteps shattered the silence.","The commander of the Imperial Guard strode into the hall from outside, drenched in sweat, his armor askew.","Behind him came dozens of heavily armored guards, all panting for breath.","Each pair of guards carried a large, heavy redwood chest wrapped in mud on their shoulders.","More than a dozen wooden chests were neatly lined up beneath the white jade steps of the Golden Hall.","Thud! Thud! Thud!","The heavy landing of each chest struck the hearts of every civil and military official present.","“Your Majesty!”","The commander of the Imperial Guard dropped to one knee, his voice trembling with excitement.","“This humble general was ordered to search the residence of the Left Censor-in-Chief. Beneath a dry well in the rear courtyard, we discovered a massive secret chamber!”","“We also unearthed a large quantity of silver that had not yet been moved from his ancestral grave!”","“In total, we confiscated... eight hundred thousand taels of silver! Among it was even the treasury silver allocated for the Jiangnan floods three years ago!”","The moment these words were spoken, the civil and military officials of the entire court were struck as if by lightning. One after another, they collapsed to the ground.","Su Zhen rose and hurried down the steps, stopping in front of the chests caked with mud.","He lifted his foot, clad in a dragon-emblazoned boot, and aimed it at the nearest wooden chest.","Then he kicked it with all his might!","With a loud crash, the lid shattered.","In an instant, the entire hall blazed with golden light.","Neatly stacked silver ingots, mixed with dazzling gold bars, nearly blinded the officials.","The treasury of Great Yuan—the poorest treasury in the realm—had suddenly grown fabulously rich.","At the moment when everyone stood speechless, stunned by the mountains of gold and silver—","On the little golden seat beside the throne, Su Yaoyao tossed aside the lamb bone she had gnawed clean.","She casually wiped her greasy little hands with a silk handkerchief. Then, from beneath her pink quilt, she pulled out an abacus made of pure gold.","Click-clack... ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍click-clack...","The crisp, lively clatter of the abacus beads rang out cheerfully through the glittering hall."]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: Your Highness, the Crown Prince has returned to the capital","paragraphs":["The evidence was irrefutable. There was no suspense left.","The upright officials who had been wailing and swearing that they would plead for the Left Censor-in-Chief just moments ago now looked like chickens strangled by the neck.","Eight hundred thousand taels of silver were laid out before them. Who would still dare say a single word of objection?","Since the founding of the Great Abyss Kingdom, they had never seen a traitor to the nation so brazenly corrupt—nor one who had stolen such an astounding fortune!","“Guards! Strip this old bastard of his official hat and peacock feathers!”","Su Zhen sat firmly upon the imperial throne. With a sweep of his hand, his voice rang out like that of Yama, come to claim a soul.","“Throw him into the Sky Prison and interrogate him thoroughly. Confiscate all his property—not a single copper coin is to be left behind!”","“And that good-for-nothing son of his—drag him back as well. Break both his legs and toss him into prison!”","The Imperial Guards surged forward.","The Left Censor-in-Chief no longer even had the strength to beg for mercy. He was dragged from the Golden Hall like a dead dog.","A glaring trail of urine streaked across the golden bricks. The old bastard had wet himself on the spot.","The Golden Hall fell utterly silent. One could hear a pin drop.","Su Zhen’s deep gaze swept over the kneeling officials below, and the corners of his lips curved into a cold smile.","“My dear ministers, who was it just now that said the Crown Princess should be deposed?”","“Step forward and let me take a good look at your so-called integrity.”","Silence.","Deathly silence.","Every official in the court wished they could bury their heads in the cracks between the golden bricks. Who would dare provoke the Tyrant at a time like this?","Even if they were given ten times their courage, no one dared mention deposing the Crown Princess again.","“Since no one has any objections, court is dismissed!”","Su Zhen rose abruptly, in an excellent mood.","This morning’s court session had removed the most disgusting poisonous fang, torn the purists’ mask from their faces, and netted him an entire mountain of gold.","It was truly exhilarating!","After court, in a side hall of the Coiled Dragon Palace.","Su Zhen looked at the mountains of wooden crates and waved his hand, making good on his promise to his daughter.","“Sweetheart, you deserve the greatest credit for what happened today!”","Su Zhen smiled so broadly that his wrinkles deepened, his eyes overflowing with affection.","After the Minister of Revenue had personally counted everything, the actual cash and land deeds confiscated from the Left Censor-in-Chief’s household—excluding the half his son had gambled away—amounted to exactly two hundred and fifty thousand taels of silver that could be deposited into the treasury immediately.","“I am a man of my word. Since I promised you a cut, I won’t go back on it!”","Su Zhen pointed at several large redwood chests. “You’ll get thirty percent of this two hundred and fifty thousand taels in cash!”","“Seventy-five ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍thousand taels. Consider it payment for your information!”","“Take it back and spend it however you like. If you run out, just tell your imperial father. I’ll go confiscate a few more officials’ estates for you!”","Seventy-five thousand taels!","Su Yaoyao stared at the gleaming silver ingots, her beautiful, peach-blossom eyes curving into two crescent moons.","[Tyrant Dad is mighty! Tyrant Dad is so generous!]","[This golden thigh is absolutely worth clinging to! He’s a walking, human-shaped money printer!]","Hearing his daughter’s straightforward praise in her thoughts, Su Zhen straightened his back proudly.","At that moment, the vanity of a doting old father was fulfilled beyond measure.","He felt that just to hear a few more thoughts like that, he could turn the entire capital upside down and confiscate every corrupt official’s estate.","“Thank you, Imperial Father! Long live the emperor! Long live the emperor! Long, long live the emperor!”","Su Yaoyao called out sweetly, then directed the Imperial Guards to move her share to the Hall of Radiant Dawn.","A grand procession of carts hauled several loads of heavy silver.","Under the envious, near-mad stares of the imperial consorts in the rear palace, the procession swaggered all the way back to the Crown Princess’s residence.","Inside the Hall of Radiant Dawn, the doors were tightly shut.","Su Yaoyao sent all the palace maids and eunuchs outside, leaving herself alone in the main hall.","She dumped all seventy-five thousand taels’ worth of banknotes, gold, and silver ingots onto the enormous rosewood canopy bed.","The bed was piled high with gold and silver, glittering so brightly it could blind a person.","Su Yaoyao let out a cheer and threw herself onto the bed.","She rolled left and right through the ocean of money, coating herself in the scent of wealth. To her, it was the finest fragrance in the world.","“I’m rich! I’m rich!”","“With this startup capital, my imperial arms factory can finally begin operations!”","Su Yaoyao sat cross-legged on the bed, a golden abacus in her hands, her little face taut with concentration.","As a top-level interstellar poison doctor and mechanic, she knew all too well that in this ancient world, even the greatest martial artist would still be afraid of a kitchen knife.","If she wanted to truly secure her position, she had to establish overwhelming firepower!","[Building a Gatling gun requires a huge amount of refined iron, and I’ll also need to buy the ingredients for smokeless gunpowder.]","[Sulfur, saltpeter, charcoal—back in ancient times, all of those things are restricted goods. I’ll have to spend a fortune sweeping up supplies on the black market.]","[And my upgraded biological poison-gas bombs will require quite a few rare medicinal ingredients too...]","Su Yaoyao calculated every expense carefully, a grand blueprint for a military-industrial empire taking shape in her mind.","Just as she was considering whether to take another stroll through the Golden Hall tomorrow and see which minister had a treasury stamped on his head—","Bang!","The doors of the Hall of Radiant Dawn were slammed open from outside.","A young palace maid in a jade-green uniform came tumbling in, crawling and rolling across the threshold.","She had been running too fast, tripped over her own feet, and landed flat on her face.","But she did not even have time to feel the pain. Using both hands and feet, she crawled across the golden bricks, her face pale as paper.","“Your Highness, the Crown Princess! This is bad! Something terrible has happened!”","The maid’s voice was choked with tears and trembled like a leaf in an autumn wind.","The golden abacus in Su Yaoyao’s hands came to a halt. She frowned.","[What happened? Did the old witch escape and come looking for me to settle the score?]","“Why are you panicking? If the sky falls, Imperial Father will hold it up.”","Su Yaoyao calmly stuffed several large-denomination banknotes into her robes, then casually picked up a solid-gold teapot beside her.","“Speak slowly. Who’s trying to steal my money?”","In Su Yaoyao’s eyes, the most important matter in the entire world right now was anyone trying to touch her money.","“N-no one is stealing your money...”","The little maid knelt on the floor, her teeth chattering. She looked as though she were speaking of some terrifying forbidden existence.","“It’s the Eastern Palace... It’s that Living Yama in the Eastern Palace!”","“Your Highness, the Crown Prince has returned to the capital!”","Su Yaoyao froze.","The Crown Prince?","Her legendary older brother, who supposedly killed without blinking, was psychologically twisted, and took pleasure in tormenting people?","As far as she knew, the Crown Prince of the Great Abyss Kingdom, Su Jin, had inherited the Tyrant Dad’s ruthlessness perfectly—and even surpassed him.","He had been sent to a frontier military camp at the age of ten. At sixteen, he had led troops in slaughtering three cities of an enemy nation. His reputation as the God of Death had shaken the entire world.","Rumor had it that he was temperamental and bloodthirsty.","His favorite pastime was to skin living people whole, turn their skins into lanterns, and hang them beneath the eaves of the Eastern Palace.","“So what if he’s returned to the capital? What does that have to do with me?”","Su Yaoyao curled her lips.","[At worst, I just won’t provoke him. We can stay out of each other’s way.]","[As long as I cling tightly to Tyrant Dad’s leg, I can quietly work on my military industry in this palace.]","“But... but just now, when I went to the imperial kitchens to fetch some pastries, I overheard people from the Secret Guard Camp whispering...”","The little maid was so frightened that tears began rolling down her cheeks. She lowered her voice as though afraid even a ghost might hear her.","“The Crown Prince returned to the capital in secret this time. He didn’t even notify His Majesty in advance!”","“And... and as soon as he entered the city, he started asking about you!”","Su Yaoyao rubbed her chin.","Asking about me?","[Could it be that he heard the imperial family had gained a younger sister and rushed back especially to bring me a welcoming gift?]","【Could This Deranged Brother Really Be Coming to See Me with a Boxful of Human Heads?】","“Your Highness, how can you still be laughing?”","The little palace maid was so frantic she kept nodding. “The Crown Prince is suspicious by nature and hates anyone else sharing His Majesty’s favor!”","“He’s heard that not only were you named Crown Princess, but you also got Noble Consort Jing placed under house arrest. He thinks you’re devious and calculating.”","“Everyone in the palace is saying that the Crown Prince is coming to the Zhaoyang Palace tonight to personally teach you a lesson!”","Teach me a lesson?","Su Yaoyao let out a cold laugh, disdain flashing in her eyes.","【Wants to teach me the rules? He should first find out what I did back in the interstellar era.】","【Let alone a Crown Prince—even if the Emperor of Heaven himself showed up, anyone who dared touch my money would walk in and be carried out!】","“All right, stop crying. You’re giving me a headache.”","Su Yaoyao waved her hand. “Go on. Eat when you’re hungry and sleep when you’re tired. And make sure every door and window in Zhaoyang Palace is tightly shut tonight.”","Seeing that Her Highness the Crown Princess was completely unfazed, the little palace maid could only wipe away her tears and leave in despair.","The Zhaoyang Palace fell silent once more, and a faint, murderous chill crept into the air.","Night descended, and dark clouds pressed down over the city.","The clear night sky suddenly erupted into a gale.","The howling northern wind sounded like the wails of ghosts and the cries of wolves, whipping the trees outside Zhaoyang Palace into a frenzy. Their shadows writhed like countless demons baring their claws and fangs.","The imperial palace was shrouded in an oppressive, deathly silence. Even the patrolling Imperial Guards hunched their shoulders and quickened their pace.","Midnight.","A faint sound came from the black glazed tiles atop Zhaoyang Palace.","It was so soft it sounded like a fallen leaf landing on the roof.","After that slight noise, a ghostlike black shadow appeared soundlessly on the ridgepole.","The gale tugged at the figure’s loose black night clothes, making them snap and billow.","The clouds parted, and a sliver of pale moonlight spilled down, illuminating the figure’s face.","It was a face concealed behind a grim, fearsome mask resembling a rakshasa with blue skin and fangs.","Through the two hollow eye sockets of the mask gleamed a pair of cold, merciless eyes, bloodthirsty as vipers.","The shadow moved with uncanny lightness, sliding silently down the roof tiles like a bat hanging upside down.","It came to hang outside the carved window of Su Yaoyao’s bedchamber.","In one hand, the shadow held an oddly shaped poisoned blade, its edge shimmering with an eerie blue light.","Several drops of thick poison blood dripped from the blade, giving off a pungent, sickly-sweet odor.","One drop. Then another.","They struck the steps outside the window, corroding several small pits into the stone.","Through the thin Korean paper covering the window, the shadow could hear the steady sound of breathing inside the chamber.","Beneath the rakshasa mask, the corners of the figure’s mouth curled into a cruel smile.","A bone-chilling, sinister laugh drifted eerily through the howling wind..."]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: You're a crown prince, so why are you using such outdated biochemical weapons","paragraphs":["The gale was like an invisible giant hand, savagely tearing at the treetops outside Zhaoyang Palace.","Its mournful howl threaded through the palace walls, like the shrieks of countless vengeful ghosts wailing in the dead of night.","Heavy clouds, black as undiluted ink, swallowed the moon’s wan light.","It was so dark that one could not see one’s own hand before one’s face. On the glazed tiles of Zhaoyang Palace, a shadow lay like a drop of ink melting into the night.","The carved agarwood window of Zhaoyang Palace was quietly unlatched from the outside.","The shadow slipped through the half-open window like a boneless venomous snake, gliding lightly into the Crown Princess’s bedchamber.","A cold wind carrying the stench of blood and decay poured into the warm, luxurious hall.","By the faint glow of the luminous pearl inside, the intruder’s true face gradually emerged from the darkness.","Beneath a mask resembling a blue-faced, fanged demon, a pair of narrow, upturned eyes gleamed without a trace of warmth.","Endless ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍cruelty and savagery swirled within them.","He was Su Jin, the Eastern Palace’s master—the Crown Prince of Great Yuan, the current Crown Prince whose name struck fear into the hearts of the surrounding kingdoms.","According to legend, at the age of ten, he had volunteered to go to the borderlands, where corpses lay strewn across the battlefield.","At sixteen, he had single-handedly charged into the enemy formation and slaughtered his way through three cities of the opposing kingdom, piling the severed heads of its generals into a nauseating monument of skulls.","Throughout the court and countryside of Great Yuan, Su Jin’s name was synonymous with the Living Yama.","He was suspicious by nature, volatile, and twisted in mind.","His favorite pastime was to take anyone who displeased him and, with the finest knife, carefully flay them alive without damaging the skin.","Then he would personally turn their skins into lanterns, hanging them high beneath the eaves of the Eastern Palace so he could admire them swaying in the wind.","And tonight, the Living Yama had secretly returned to the capital.","He had not even gone to pay his respects to the emperor. The moment he entered the palace, he had headed straight for Zhaoyang Palace.","Because he had heard that his tyrant father had actually picked up a bastard from a filthy underground black market.","Not only had he acknowledged her as his biological daughter, he had even made her the Crown Princess!","For the sake of this bastard girl, he had confined Noble Consort Jing—the woman who governed the imperial harem—to her palace.","The thought filled Su Jin with immeasurable irritation.","It was the fury of someone whose territory had been invaded.","What he hated most was having someone share the power and attention that belonged to the imperial family of Great Yuan.","Even if that someone was his “younger sister.”","Su Jin stood by the window, reached back, and slammed it shut. Then he dropped the heavy ironwood bar into place.","Click. Click.","The sound of the lock was unnervingly clear in the silent hall.","He intended to seal the chamber completely, turning it into a place where one could cry out to Heaven and receive no answer, call upon the earth and find no help.","Su Jin turned around and strolled leisurely across the hall, stepping over gold and silver jewelry scattered across the floor as he made his way deeper inside.","Seeing the vulgar golden glare filling the room, the corners of his mouth curled beneath his mask in a contemptuous sneer.","What a vulgar, greedy, idiotic street urchin.","Did she really think that with the emperor’s favor and this pile of worthless trinkets, she could survive in the man-eating imperial palace?","Tonight, he would personally teach this ignorant little sister a proper lesson in the rules of the Great Yuan imperial family.","He would turn her into a new prey he could torment and kill at will.","Su Jin’s steps halted before the rosewood canopy bed.","Through the layers of gauzy curtains, he saw the small mound beneath the covers.","Su Yaoyao lay sprawled on her back atop a pile of banknotes, sleeping utterly defenseless.","She rolled over contentedly and smacked her lips.","At the sight of that innocent, guileless sleeping face, the savagery in Su Jin’s eyes burned even more fiercely.","What he loved most was watching fresh, hopeful lives slowly broken in his hands.","Watching them collapse in terror, begging for mercy with tears streaming down their faces.","The pleasure of controlling another person’s life and death was more addictive to him than any drug.","Clang.","A dangerous scrape of metal sounded beside the bed.","Su Jin raised his right hand.","From the wide black sleeve of his robe, he drew a strangely shaped dagger with a wavy blade.","The dagger had been soaked in poison for countless days and nights. Its edge reflected no light, and a ghastly blue vapor of venom coiled around it.","Su Jin bent down, bringing with him the heavy stench of blood, and moved closer to the sleeping Su Yaoyao.","With a hand pale as death, he hooked aside the edge of her quilt.","Then he pressed the cold, poison-coated dagger against the skin over her carotid artery.","The icy touch, carrying the chill of deadly venom, seeped through her skin and into her bloodstream.","All it would take was the slightest jerk of his wrist to slice open her fragile throat.","Once the poison took effect, her body would rot from the inside out, and she would die screaming in agony.","But Su Jin had no intention of ending the game so simply.","A prey that died too quickly was boring.","With his left hand, he produced a delicate white jade wine cup as if by magic.","It was filled with a thick, pitch-black liquid resembling ink.","Strange black bubbles continuously rose to the surface.","Glug... glug...","As the bubbles burst, they released a peculiar fragrance so sweet it was nauseating.","This was an unparalleled poison: Thousand-Gut Dissolver.","Anyone who drank it would suffer ruptured intestines and shattered organs. Every bone in their body would twist and break one inch at a time.","In the end, their entire body would curl head to toe into a ring, and they would wail in agony for three days and three nights before finally dying.","This was the greeting gift he had prepared for his new little sister.","Su Jin looked down at the little girl on the bed.","He imagined her reaction.","She would awaken to the cold blade at her throat.","She would see the demon-like mask.","She would smell the sweet, deathly fragrance of the poisoned wine.","Then those beautiful eyes would fly open in terror.","Her whole body would tremble. Tears would pour down her face, and she would scream and beg for mercy.","At the thought, a low laugh rose from Su Jin’s throat, chilling enough to make one’s blood run cold.","“Good little sister, wake up.”","Su Jin’s voice was cold as ice, like a chilling wind blowing from the deepest pits of the Netherworld. It held not the slightest trace of warmth.","He brought the cup of black, vaporous poison to Su Yaoyao’s lips.","The rim of the cup touched her soft mouth.","“Drink it.”","His tone was gentle, as though he were coaxing a baby to sleep, yet the murderous intent in his words was enough to freeze the air.","“Your brother promises you this cup will make your death completely painless.”","Silence.","A deathly stillness settled over the canopy bed.","Su Jin waited patiently.","He waited for the prey’s scream upon awakening, waited for the exquisite expression of despair and supplication.","Time seemed to freeze.","At last, the little girl on the bed moved.","Su Yaoyao’s eyelashes trembled twice.","Slowly, she opened her clear, peach-blossom eyes.","There was no scream, no trembling—not even a single tear of fear.","She simply lay there, calm and composed, glancing first at the dagger pressed against her throat.","Then she looked at Su Jin’s blue-faced, fanged mask.","Finally, her gaze fell upon the black poison at her lips.","Su Yaoyao frowned.","Her expression was complicated, as though she were looking at an incurable idiot, and she stared at Su Jin.","The sight left the murderous Eastern Palace’s Living Yama completely dumbfounded.","What kind of reaction was this?","Had she been frightened senseless?","Could she not even cry?","Just as Su Jin, filled with confusion, tightened his grip on the dagger and prepared to draw a little blood to clear Su Yaoyao’s head—","something unexpected happened.","Su Yaoyao, who had remained motionless until then, suddenly extended her small hand.","Her movement was astonishingly fast, swift as lightning.","Whoosh!","Su Yaoyao snatched the white jade wine cup from Su Jin’s hand!","The movement was so rough that a few drops of the poisoned wine sloshed out, splattering onto the expensive sable-fur blanket and burning several black holes into it.","Su Jin froze.","He had roamed the martial world, massacred cities, and killed countless people over the years, but he had never seen anyone willingly snatch poison away from him.","Had she realized that death was inevitable and was simply in a hurry to be on her way?","After taking the poisoned wine, Su Yaoyao did not gulp it down in despair, as Su Jin had expected.","Instead, she wrinkled her little nose in distaste and held the wine beneath it.","Then, as though she were inspecting a piece of trash, she gave it a forceful sniff.","A deafening voice, filled with boundless contempt, suddenly exploded in Su Jin’s mind!","【That’s it?!】","【You dare present this stuff as poison and use it to kill people?!】","【The purity is ridiculously low! It’s packed with impurities—one look is enough to tell it was crudely brewed using some primitive method. It’s nothing but inferior garbage!】","【You’re the Crown Prince, yet this is the outdated biochemical weapon you’re using?】","【There are at least a dozen kinds of incompletely reacted plant fibers and heavy-metal impurities mixed in.】","【Drink this rubbish, and forget about having your insides corroded—it’ll cause, at most, a gastrointestinal disorder and make you spend three days running to the latrine!】","【Sigh. The ancient study of poisons really is hopelessly backward. What a disappointment!】","Su Jin’s face, hidden beneath the mask of the fierce deity, stiffened like stone.","Beneath the mask, his pupils abruptly contracted upon hearing those thoughts..."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: Haven't even managed to inflict a scratch yet","paragraphs":["What had he just heard?","This wild girl was actually dismissing his miraculous poison as some cheap, defective knockoff?","And she even knew what was in it.","What terrified him most was that this girl’s inner voice could worm its way into his mind!","Su Jin’s brain short-circuited.","On the bed, Su Yaoyao looked like a traveler who had spent three days and three nights dying of thirst in the desert before suddenly spotting a glass of ice-cold soda.","She tipped her head back and poured the entire cup of Thousand-Gut poison wine into her mouth!","“Gulp! ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Gulp!”","The sound of swallowing echoed through the silent Zhaoyang Hall.","Su Yaoyao drank with astonishing boldness and efficiency.","A cup of deadly poison powerful enough to kill an elephant was emptied into her stomach without leaving behind a single drop.","When she finished, she even smacked her lips regretfully.","She stuck out her tender pink tongue and licked the black poison still clinging to the corners of her mouth.","“The flavor’s a little weak. It tastes like watered-down, expired herbal tea. Not nearly stimulating enough.”","Su Yaoyao wiped her mouth carelessly with her sleeve, then patted her little belly in satisfaction.","“Burp.”","A loud, long belch rang out.","A tiny black bubble carrying a faintly sweet, fishy odor floated out of Su Yaoyao’s mouth. It popped in midair with a sharp snap.","Su Jin nearly popped, too.","He stood there like a stone statue, still holding the poisoned dagger aloft in a daze.","That was Thousand-Gut Powder!","It was the poison the Western Regions’ imperial family used to execute rebellious ministers!","A single drop was enough to tear the intestines apart, make blood pour from all seven orifices, and leave its victim howling in agony before dying a horrible death.","And this wild girl had downed it like tea?!","How was that possible?","There was absolutely no one in this world who could withstand the poison’s effects!","Su Jin tightened his grip on the dagger, forcing down the shock and absurdity surging through his heart.","He stared coldly at Su Yaoyao on the bed and spoke through clenched teeth, his voice icy.","“Stop putting on an act and pretending to be some kind of mystic.”","“Once the Thousand-Gut poison wine enters your throat, not even an immortal can save you.”","Su Jin’s eyes turned vicious as he watched Su Yaoyao’s face.","“Before I count to three, you’ll feel your internal organs being scorched by raging fire.”","“You’ll watch helplessly as blood pours from your seven orifices, until you turn into a foul-smelling puddle of pus.”","Su Jin loved counting down to death.","There was an indescribable pleasure in looking down from above and savoring the desperate struggle of prey in its final moments.","“Three!”","Su Jin spat out the first number.","Su Yaoyao showed no reaction whatsoever. She merely shifted into a more comfortable position and leaned against the soft pillow.","“Two!”","Su Jin stared at the corners of Su Yaoyao’s eyes and mouth, waiting for black blood to spill out.","Su Yaoyao gave a bored yawn and looked at him as though he were an idiot.","“One!”","As the final number fell, a cruel smile curled up at the corners of Su Jin’s mouth.","Die.","Howl in agony!","One second passed.","Then two.","...","Nothing happened in Zhaoyang Hall.","Su Yaoyao had not even suffered so much as a scratch. In fact, because the inferior poison wine contained certain herbs that promoted blood circulation, her fair little face had taken on a healthy flush.","She looked even more energetic than before she drank the poison!","The air froze in awkward silence.","Sitting on the bed, Su Yaoyao propped her chin in both hands and blinked her limpid, peach-blossom eyes at Su Jin.","“Um... Brother Crown Prince.”","Her tone was completely innocent, with even a hint of sympathy, as she asked:","“Did someone cheat you at the black market?”","“The fake medicine you bought is way too low-quality. Other than making me feel like I need to use the toilet, it couldn’t even give me a superficial wound.”","Her words landed like a resounding slap, viciously striking the face of the Great Yuan’s Living Yama.","Behind his mask, Su Jin’s face turned the color of pig liver.","Fake medicine?!","He was the Crown Prince of Great Yuan, the Eastern Palace’s God of Death, a man whose very name inspired terror.","And he had been cheated by a medicine peddler at the black market, buying a cup of fake poison wine to murder someone?!","What!","Utter!","Humiliation!","No wonder this wild girl had dared to gulp it down. She must have seen right away that the poison was fake!","Rage and humiliation surged like a violent hurricane, obliterating Su Jin’s reason.","“Since the poison can’t kill you, I’ll personally skin you alive!”","Su Jin had been provoked. He no longer had the patience to toy with his prey.","He was going to use his blade to chop this bastard who dared mock him into mincemeat—right here, right now!","“Whoosh!”","A shrill sound split the air.","The wave-shaped poisoned blade in Su Jin’s hand transformed into a streak of dark-blue lightning.","It shot straight toward Su Yaoyao’s slender throat!","He held nothing back in this strike. It was a pure killing move.","He wanted to watch Su Yaoyao spray blood everywhere, her head severed from her body!","Faced with the lightning-fast fatal attack, a disdainful, mocking smile tugged at the corners of Su Yaoyao’s mouth.","Thinking of using a blade? You really think I’m a pushover?","Just as the dark-blue blade tip came within half an inch of Su Yaoyao’s throat, she moved.","Her upper body tilted sharply to the left at an angle that defied human anatomy.","The poisoned blade grazed her neck and narrowly missed.","Her seemingly boneless little hand shot out like a striking viper.","Smack!","The crisp sound of bone meeting bone rang out.","Su Yaoyao clamped down on Su Jin’s right wrist—the hand holding the blade.","Her thumb and forefinger locked onto the ulnar nerve at the most vulnerable point of his wrist.","A sharp, numbing pain swept through Su Jin’s right arm.","His right hand suddenly went limp, and his five fingers lost all strength.","Clang.","The dagger coated in deadly poison fell uselessly onto the footboard of the canopy bed.","Su Jin was horrified beyond belief!","He was one of the Great Yuan’s most formidable experts!","Even the chief eunuch of the imperial palace would never have been able to disarm him so easily.","Yet this little girl before him had crippled his right arm with just two fingers?!","What kind of sorcery was this?!","Before Su Jin could recover, Su Yaoyao’s counterattack descended like a sudden storm.","“There’s a saying: courtesy demands that favors be returned.”","Su Yaoyao’s voice was clear and sweet, yet carried a streak of innocent wickedness.","“Brother fed me such awful fake wine. Now it’s little sister’s turn to feed you!”","Before she finished speaking, Su Yaoyao gave his arm a sharp pull.","Using the momentum, she launched herself into the air.","Her left hand moved with lightning speed, gripping the joint of Su Jin’s lower jaw.","Then she wrenched it downward!","Crack!","Su Jin’s jaw was forcibly pried open.","At some point, a perfectly round pill the size of a small ball had appeared in Su Yaoyao’s right palm.","It had no medicinal fragrance. Instead, it gave off a strange, faint glow.","This was an interstellar specialty that Su Yaoyao had just exchanged for from her personal military-tech vault.","Truth Serum—Flashing Fluorescent Edition!","“Swallow this!”","Su Yaoyao stuffed the pill into Su Jin’s wide-open mouth.","With her left hand, she slapped his chin shut.","Gulp.","Under Su Yaoyao’s smooth, rapid sequence of violent maneuvers, Su Jin had no time to react.","His Adam’s apple bobbed once, and the strange pill slid down his esophagus into his stomach.","After finishing, Su Yaoyao sprang lightly backward like a nimble cat and landed steadily at the other end of the bed.","She dusted off her hands and watched Su Jin with an expectant expression.","The pill entered his stomach.","A monstrous fury and murderous intent erupted in Su Jin’s eyes.","He had been ambushed by a little girl—and forced to swallow some unknown substance!","“You’re courting death!”","Su Jin roared and sat down cross-legged, circulating the pure qi within his body.","He was going to force the strange poisonous pill out with his internal energy!","But in the very next instant, Su Jin’s expression changed.","The qi he took such pride in was completely useless!","A strange current of heat pierced through his internal organs and spread through every meridian in his body like a wildfire.","“What... is this...?”","Cold sweat beaded across Su Jin’s forehead beneath his mask.","He lowered his head and stared in shock at his hands.","In the bleak moonlight, Su Jin was horrified to discover that his paper-pale hands had undergone a bizarre transformation.","A faint, eerie glow radiated from beneath his skin!","It was dazzling, outrageously garish, and utterly devastatingly...","Barbie-pink fluorescence!","Su Jin’s cold, merciless heart of a killer, hard as stone, shattered into powder.","He looked up and stared through his mask of blue-green fangs at the girl in the corner of the bed, who was grinning like a little demon.","His voice was filled with terror and despair.","“You... What kind of monster did you make me eat?!”"]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Only by holding my little pink bunny can I dare to close my eyes.","paragraphs":["The dim Barbie-pink fluorescence spread like a living virus.","Starting from Su Jin’s wrist, it raced across his entire body at a terrifying speed visible to the naked eye.","In the space of a few short moments, his black nightwear had completely lost its purpose as a disguise.","From head to toe, he had transformed into a gigantic, blindingly bright pink human-shaped lightbulb!","The dazzling pink glow illuminated every corner of the Zhaoyang Palace.","The heaps of gold and silver treasures piled on the bed were all cast in a rosy halo.","Even Su Jin’s long, sleek black hair stood straight up strand by strand, radiating an eye-searing pink light.","The terrifying, sinister hannya mask covering his face—complete with its blue visage and savage fangs—looked inexplicably adorable under the pink fluorescence.","“You’re courting death!”","Su Jin was so mortified and furious that he nearly lost his mind. He was the Crown Prince of Dayuan, the Eastern Palace’s Living Yama—how could he possibly endure such humiliation?!","He raised his hand, preparing to smash the little wild girl’s skull with a single palm strike.","But the instant his foot touched the floor, Su Jin discovered in horror that his legs were no longer obeying him!","The toes of his left foot touched the ground as his right foot slid smoothly backward.","Then the toes of his right foot touched the ground as his left foot slid smoothly backward.","In the silent bedchamber of the Crown Princess, the most ruthless killer in the entire Dayuan Empire was gliding backward.","He was doing the moonwalk!","“What... what is going on?! My legs!”","Su Jin slid across the floor, roaring in despair.","He wanted to move forward and snap the little girl’s neck, but his body insisted on going in the opposite direction.","Paired with the eye-searing Barbie-pink glow covering his entire body, the sight was so ridiculous that Su Yaoyao sat on the bed, clutching her stomach and laughing until tears nearly streamed from her eyes.","[Oh my gosh, the Frenzied Dance Fruit really is as incredible as they say!]","[That silky-smooth moonwalk, that perfectly timed gliding! What a waste—he should’ve debuted in a boy band!]","[The cold-blooded killer can dance? The contrast is adorable! Keep sliding, keep it coming!]","Just as Su Jin was moonwalking and questioning every decision that had led him to this moment, a series of hurried, heavy footsteps sounded outside the Zhaoyang Palace.","It was Su Zhen.","Although he had returned to the imperial study, Su Zhen was still worried about his precious daughter.","He was too excited to sleep anyway, so he had simply taken his sword and gone for a stroll around the Zhaoyang Palace.","The muffled roars coming from inside the palace immediately set his keen senses on edge.","“Damn it! An assassin!”","Su Zhen’s eyes nearly bulged from their sockets. He had only just managed to find his precious money tree of a daughter—there was no way he would let anything happen to her!","Without calling for anyone, he drew the Longquan sword from his waist.","Then he strode toward the entrance of the Zhaoyang Palace and kicked the doors with all his might.","Bang!","The heavy palace doors were kicked to pieces, sending splinters flying everywhere.","“What scoundrel dares to assassinate My Crown Princess?! Prepare to die!”","Su Zhen roared with earth-shaking force, his imperial killing aura surging violently as he charged inside.","He never could have imagined that what awaited him would be a flood of Barbie-pink light pollution so intense it made his retinas want to kill themselves.","The moment the doors opened, the dense pink fluorescence poured out of the palace like a flash flood.","Caught completely off guard, Su Zhen was stabbed by the light until his vision went black.","He raised his broad sleeve to shield his eyes, and tears sprang from them.","“What kind of demonic magic is this?! What in the world is that thing?!”","Forcing himself to endure the stinging pain, Su Zhen peered through the gap in his sleeve and finally saw what was happening inside.","Then—","the well-traveled Emperor of Dayuan turned to stone.","An assassin covered in pink light and wearing a hannya mask was gliding backward with a bizarre gait that Su Zhen had never seen in his entire life.","When Su Jin saw his father charge in with a sword, the humiliation burning inside him reached its peak.","He wanted to explain. He wanted to say that he was the Crown Prince, not some assassin.","But the Truth Serum had taken effect!","The truth serum from the interstellar era did more than force people to tell the truth. It also magnified their inner weaknesses and their urge to pour out their feelings without limit.","Su Jin moonwalked all the way to the middle of the hall, where he reached a coiled-dragon pillar.","He could no longer hold himself back. He threw his arms around the thick golden nanmu pillar.","He clung to it desperately, like a drowning man grasping a lifeline.","Then, with a loud sob, the Eastern Palace’s Living Yama—the man who killed without batting an eye—began wailing like a three-year-old child who had been deeply wronged.","Tears streamed down from beneath his terrifying mask like beads from a broken string.","“Waaah... Father!”","Su Jin hiccupped between sobs, forced to shout at the top of his lungs.","Though his voice was thick with tears, his internal energy carried it clearly throughout the hall.","Su Zhen’s hand froze in midair, still clutching his sword. His jaw nearly dropped to the floor.","That voice, that figure...","Why did they look so much like his cold-blooded, heartless Crown Prince?!","“Father! I never wanted to kill anyone! Waaah!”","Su Jin hugged the pillar and cried his heart out.","“Those human-skin lanterns were fake! They were made from pigskin! I’m even afraid to kill a chicken!”","“I pretend to be the Living Yama every day because I’m too scared to talk to other people!”","His words crashed into the Zhaoyang Palace like thunder from the heavens.","The Longquan sword slipped from Su Zhen’s hand and clanged against the floor.","He stared, dumbfounded, at the pink glowing figure sobbing uncontrollably around the pillar.","Afraid to kill a chicken?!","This was the God-of-Slaughter Crown Prince of Dayuan, the one who had shaken the neighboring kingdoms and commanded a massive army?!","But the power of the truth serum didn’t end there.","Su Jin’s urge to confess continued to surge wildly, and his mouth simply refused to stop.","“Waaah... I don’t want to go fight at the frontier either! I get dizzy when I see blood!”","“When I sleep at night, I can’t fall asleep if there’s no light in the tent!”","“Every night, I have to hug my pink little bunny plushie before I dare close my eyes!”","“Waaah, Father! My little sister bullies me! She made me drink poison and turned me into a giant lightbulb!”","Silence.","A deathly silence.","The only sound echoing through the hall was Su Jin’s heart-rending wailing.","At some point, Su Yaoyao had acquired a handful of sunflower seeds. Sitting on the bed, she cracked them with great relish.","[Holy crap! This is explosive!]","[The legendary Eastern Palace’s God of Death is actually a coward who’s terrified of everything—and a severe social-phobe who has to hug a pink little bunny plushie to sleep?!]","[Were people in ancient times really this good at pretending?]","Hearing Su Yaoyao’s thoughts, Su Zhen finally came back to himself.","He looked at his son, who was hugging the pillar, glowing all over with pink light, and crying like a complete idiot.","Su Zhen’s face shifted from green to white and back again. In the end, he couldn’t hold it in any longer.","Pfft!","The Tyrant of Dayuan burst out laughing in front of both his children.","“Hahahaha! A pink little bunny?!”","Su Zhen laughed so hard he could barely straighten his back. “You little rebel! You’ve pretended to be cold and ruthless for over a decade!”","“I thought you were truly a heartless God of Death! Who would’ve guessed you were just a scared little bunny who’s afraid of the dark!”","The more Su Zhen thought about it, the more absurd it seemed, and the louder he laughed. He was even happier than he had been earlier, when he had seized eight hundred thousand taels of silver.","“That pink glow suits your little bunny perfectly!”","Listening to his father’s completely unrestrained mockery and his sister’s nonstop mental barrage of ridicule, Su Jin’s heart shattered into dust.","He felt as though his soul had already left his body.","Perhaps leaving this glowing shell behind was for the best.","He released the pillar. His legs went weak, and he slid down along it.","Under the lingering effects of the potion, he split his legs on the smooth golden-brick floor.","Su ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Jin lay sprawled on the ground in a full split, his entire body still glowing Barbie pink.","Beneath the mask, his eyes were utterly devoid of hope, as if he had seen through the mortal world and was ready to ascend into nirvana on the spot.","He had it so hard.","The terrifying image he had painstakingly cultivated for more than a decade...","Was utterly—completely—ruined tonight!","A tearing pain shot through his inner thigh, but compared with the devastation to his dignity, this bit of physical pain was nothing.","To salvage the last shred of dignity he possessed as the Crown Prince of Dayuan, and to make this heartless father and daughter stop laughing,","Su Jin bit through the tip of his tongue, using the sharp pain to briefly suppress the effects of the truth serum.","He raised his head. His eyes were bloodshot as he glared at Su Zhen, gritting his teeth before roaring,","“Imperial Father, stop laughing!”","“I secretly returned to the capital this time because I intercepted an extremely confidential report!”","“Someone in the imperial court has colluded with foreign enemies. In three days, during the Mid-Autumn night banquet, they intend to use ten cartloads of black gunpowder...”","“To blow the Taiji Hall sky-high!”"]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: Sister, open your eyes and look at me","paragraphs":["With any normal emperor, he would probably have collapsed to the floor by now, his face drained of color as he frantically summoned the Imperial Guard to protect him.","But Su Zhen was not normal.","The Tyrant of Dayuan rose calmly to his feet and smoothed the wrinkles from his robe.","He rubbed his clean-shaven chin, and an indescribable excitement flashed through his deep-set eyes.","Blow ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍up the Hall of Supreme Polarity?","Would this finally give those civil officials who argued in court every day and gave him a headache a change of scenery?","Su Zhen looked at the Crown Prince, who was doing a full split on the floor, then at Su Yaoyao, who sat by the bed with an expression of utter calm.","“Ten carts of black powder. That’s quite a lot.”","Su Zhen spoke in a deep, steady voice.","“If it went off inside the hall, at least half the imperial palace would collapse.”","He turned his head toward Su Yaoyao, his eyes asking a question.","The moment Su Yaoyao heard “ten carts of black powder,” her entire being perked up.","Her bright, sparkling peach-blossom eyes lit up like tiny lightbulbs, blazing with greed.","[Holy crap! Ten carts of black powder?!]","[I wasn’t hearing things, was I? When you’re sleepy, someone really does send you a pillow!]","Su Yaoyao screamed inwardly, while the abacus beads in her mind clicked furiously, throwing off sparks.","[I was just worrying that the ancient steelmaking process was progressing too slowly, and I still couldn’t get the propellant for my Gatling gun worked out!]","[These villains are actually amazing. Wow, they’re being so considerate.]","[If I can get my hands on all ten carts of black powder, then I’ll have more than enough of the raw materials needed to build a hand-cranked Gatling gun, won’t I?!]","[By then, I won’t have just one gun. I’ll be able to assemble an entire mobile artillery position!]","[Forget one Hall of Supreme Polarity—even blasting a hole through the city wall would be a piece of cake!]","Hearing Su Yaoyao’s passionate battle plans, the smile on Su Zhen’s face grew even wider.","His usually cold features now held a trace of something else...","The satisfaction of a proud father.","His precious daughter truly had lofty ambitions.","A heaven-sent military supplies gift pack—refusing it would be inviting a lightning strike.","Su Zhen strode over to Su Jin, who was still stuck in his split, and looked down at him.","“You heard her.”","“Since they’ve prepared so many wonderful things for us, wouldn’t it be rude of us, as the hosts, not to go inspect the delivery? We’d be letting all their hard work go to waste.”","Su Jin remained kneeling on the floor, questioning his entire existence.","He looked at his glowing pink hands, then at this father-and-daughter pair who refused to follow any normal script.","He wondered if he was still dreaming—or if the poison had damaged his brain.","Was this how a family was supposed to react?","This was treason!","A crime punishable by the extermination of the entire clan!","Why were they acting so excited?!","“Wait... Father, Little Sister...”","Su Jin clawed at his hair in despair, his normally icy voice weak and listless.","“That’s ten carts of gunpowder! There are also countless flammable arrows and barrels of oil mixed in!”","“Once it goes off, forget the imperial palace—the entire capital will suffer!”","Su Yaoyao had no time for this sheltered brother who had clearly never seen the world.","She hopped down from the bed, ran over barefoot, and generously patted Su Jin’s stiff shoulder.","“Brother, your perspective is too narrow.”","Su Yaoyao shook her head with complete seriousness. Her little-adult expression made the corner of Su Jin’s eye twitch violently.","“When it comes to life, the most important thing is to broaden your horizons.”","“They’re preparing to blow us up, which means they’re delivering materials to us.”","“Not only are we going to accept the entire shipment, we’re going to teach them a lesson in return.”","Su Yaoyao turned to Su Zhen. The two exchanged a glance.","Their eyes held exactly the same expression—","the greedy excitement of predators.","Father and daughter reached a tacit understanding without saying a word.","It was benevolent to the point of being terrifying.","Su Yaoyao turned back and flashed her foolish brother a dazzling smile.","“Brother, instead of standing here looking like someone died, why don’t we go rob a road together?”","“Don’t worry. As long as you stick with your little sister, I guarantee you’ll see enough gunpowder, steel, and rare ores to make your eyes spin.”","“And I still have plenty of good stuff in my laboratory.”","“Powders that make people dance, candies that make people tell the truth, incense that makes people repeat themselves on the spot—I guarantee every day will be thrilling!”","The corner of Su Jin’s mouth twitched even harder.","Stick with her?","Test poisons every day?","He looked at Su Yaoyao’s adorable, delicately sculpted face, and a chill shot from the soles of his feet straight to the crown of his head.","He was a pervert! A killer! A living King of Hell!","He was not a lab rat!","He wanted to refuse. He wanted to preserve the last scraps of his stubborn dignity.","But when he met Su Zhen’s intensely warning gaze and Su Yaoyao’s expectant eyes, Su Jin lowered his head tearfully.","His voice was barely louder than a mosquito’s.","“...Fine.”","The moment her brother agreed, Su Yaoyao’s smile blossomed.","She charged back to the space beneath the bed and rummaged through the pile of miscellaneous junk.","Before long, she dragged out two sets of black, gleaming night clothes.","The fabric was of exceptional quality, giving off a faint, nonslip, antistatic sheen.","Su Yaoyao flung the larger set of night clothes at Su Jin’s face, which was still glowing Barbie pink.","“Put it on.”","Her command was crisp and decisive.","Su Jin caught the clothes and stared at the night outfit with his sparkling pink eyes.","His dignity, already shattered into dust, let out one final wail.","“Change clothes?!”","Su Jin clutched the outfit.","“Little Sister, open your eyes and look at me!”","“I’m glowing from head to toe!”","“No matter what kind of night clothes I put on, it won’t make any difference!”","Su Jin was almost laughing from sheer exasperation.","If he went outside like this, every rat within a ten-mile radius would be dazzled into hibernating early.","Seeing that Su Jin was on the verge of breaking down, a mischievous glint flashed through Su Yaoyao’s eyes.","She slowly bent down and pulled another incredibly sturdy black sack from beneath the bed.","Inside it, she had stuffed thick layers of specially made light-blocking fabric.","“If you’re glowing, then just cover it up.”","Without changing expression, Su Yaoyao pulled the enormous black sack over Su Jin’s head.","She considerately adjusted the two eyeholes she had cut into it.","“It’s fine. Once you put the sack on, no one will be able to see you.”","“As long as you don’t speak, no one will know who you are.”","Su Jin stared at the large black sack in front of him, which smelled faintly of mildew.","Somewhere deep inside him, he heard something snap.","That something was called dignity.","That something was called the dignity of the imperial family.","He, the dignified Crown Prince, was actually going to wear a torn sack over his head one day?","Su Yaoyao gave Su Jin no time to refuse. She changed into her night clothes and fastened a homemade grenade to her waist.","“Stop dawdling, my dear brother.”","She dragged another handcart out from beneath the bed. It was neatly stacked with all kinds of bizarre equipment.","“Our target tonight is the Black Wind Stronghold, reputed to have defenses as solid as a fortress.”","“If we’re late, they’ll have moved all the gunpowder away.”","“Then not only will you fail to earn any credit, you won’t even get the chance to assist me!”","Su Yaoyao expertly pushed the handcart and strode toward the door.","She left Su Jin with only a resolute back to look at.","Su Jin drew a deep breath. Even though he desperately wanted to bash his head against the wall and end it all, he could only resign himself to fate and tug at the black sack over his head.","He staggered to his feet, the pink glow covering his body following him like a shadow in the night.","“Tonight’s target... the Black Wind Stronghold...”","Su Jin muttered to himself, his voice filled with deep helplessness and despair.","Then he lifted his leg, which was still doing the moonwalk.","One step, two steps, a sidestep, a turn.","Draped in dazzling Barbie pink, she stepped resolutely into the howling darkness.","Outside the main hall, the gale still raged.","Countless dead branches whipped wildly in the wind, their scraping and rubbing producing one heart-pounding sound after another.","Su Yaoyao pushed the little cart at the very front, her steps light and brisk, as if she were heading off on a spring outing.","Su Jin followed behind. With every step, he had to struggle against his uncooperative body.","Bathed in a pink glow, he looked like a moving Milky Way in the darkness.","Pushing the cart, Su Yaoyao waved to Lightbulb Brother behind her without even turning her head.","“Let’s go!”"]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: You're Almost Putting Half the Mountain's Fireflies to Shame","paragraphs":["Blackwind Stronghold, in the northern outskirts of the capital.","The stronghold lay deep within the mountains and forests, surrounded by sheer cliffs. It was easy to defend and nearly impossible to attack.","The gates of the stronghold had been built from hundreds of stacked logs, while torches stood along the walls at five-step intervals.","Night had fallen. The cold wind howled.","Along the narrow path outside the stronghold, two figures were moving swiftly under the cover of scattered rocks and shrubs, crouching low.","The little girl in front moved as lightly as a falling leaf.","She deftly climbed over a pile of rocks, moving so quickly that she did not even disturb the treetops.","Behind her, an unknown creature with a black burlap sack over its head looked especially ridiculous.","Although its head was covered, its exposed neck and shoulders glowed with an eerie Barbie-pink light, like neon.","In the pitch-black mountains, that pink glow was even more conspicuous than a lighthouse.","“Brother, could you tone it down a little?”","Su Yaoyao lowered her voice, her tone helpless. “You’re practically outshining half the fireflies on the mountain.”","With the sack over his head, Su Jin glowed with every step he took. Every now and then, he even seemed eager to break into a moonwalk.","He was so miserable he wanted to bang his head against a wall. Lowering his voice, he replied, “Can you really blame me? The potion hasn’t worn off yet!”","“And this lousy sack isn’t helping. The light is practically burning through it!”","Su Yaoyao’s lips twitched.","She pulled a metal disk resembling a compass from her robes.","It was an interstellar detector from her personal storage space.","A pale blue ripple pulsed at the center of the disk as it scanned the vital signs in the vicinity.","“Stop whining. There are two guards fifty meters to the left ahead. They’re dozing off.”","Su Yaoyao made a hand signal, indicating that Su Jin should follow closely.","She lightly leaped onto a massive rock, her eyes sharp as lightning.","With the aid of the interstellar detector, Blackwind Stronghold’s defensive layout was completely exposed to Su Yaoyao.","Every hidden sentry post, trap, and concealed guard was marked on the detector’s screen as a red dot.","“These idiots actually set the trap two meters away. Who are they trying to stop?”","Su Yaoyao gave a disdainful smile and led Su Jin around a trench filled with spikes.","Following behind his sister, Su Jin was too stunned for words.","He had thought that his illegitimate sister was merely relying on the Tyrant Emperor’s favor to behave recklessly.","But after witnessing Su Yaoyao’s ability to evade ambushes, Su Jin’s entire view of her changed.","Even the finest scouts stationed at the border could not match these skills.","“Little sis, what exactly is that treasure of yours?”","Unable to hold back any longer, Su Jin asked in a low voice. There was now a hint of awe in his tone.","Without looking back, Su Yaoyao climbed over a fence.","“Don’t ask questions. When we get back, you can be my test subject. These gadgets will keep you entertained for the rest of your life.”","The two moved one after the other, avoiding every hidden sentry as they silently approached the heart of Blackwind Stronghold.","Ahead stood a huge stone warehouse.","It was the vital stockpile where the Grand General stored his gunpowder.","Heavy iron chains coiled around the warehouse’s outer walls. Several Blackwind Stronghold bandits stood nearby with wine bottles in hand, cursing and grumbling.","“This damned wind is freezing. Who knows how much longer the Grand General is going to make us guard these jars?”","“Stop complaining. I heard we’re going to pull off something big on the night of the Mid-Autumn Festival. When that happens, we’ll be heroes!”","Crouching behind a section of broken wall, Su Yaoyao’s eyes lit up with excitement.","At last! As long as I blow this place to pieces, let’s see what that Grand General can use to start a rebellion!","She exchanged a glance with Su Jin, and the two slowly approached the warehouse doors.","Su Yaoyao took a thermal cutting torch from her storage space and prepared to cut through the iron chains.","Just as she was about to touch the lock—","A sudden burst of heavy, chaotic footsteps came from the woods to the side.","Boots crushed dead branches with loud snaps.","Su Yaoyao’s expression shifted. She grabbed Su Jin and pulled him back into the shadows.","On the detector, dozens of red dots were converging from every direction.","It was a well-trained assassin squad.","Every member wore black scale armor and carried a long, poisoned blade.","They were the Blood Drip Squad, the unit the Grand General was proudest of.","Leading the squad was a sinister-looking man with one eye.","The One-Eyed Dragon was conducting a routine patrol with his men when they happened to spot the unusual glow outside the warehouse.","The One-Eyed Dragon stopped and raised his right hand. The squad immediately spread out into an encircling formation.","“Who goes there?”","The One-Eyed Dragon shouted harshly, fixing his gaze on the patch of pink light.","“How dare you trespass in Blackwind Stronghold! You’ve got some nerve!”","“Come out, all of you, or you’ll be killed without mercy!”","Since ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍their whereabouts had been exposed, Su Yaoyao decided there was no point in hiding any longer.","She tugged at her night clothes, then reached over and yanked the ridiculous black sack off Su Jin’s head.","The dazzling Barbie-pink glow radiating from Su Jin instantly illuminated the entire warehouse.","The light was so intense that the assassins nearby could barely keep their eyes open. They staggered backward several steps.","“What... what kind of monster is that?!”","The One-Eyed Dragon was shaken to the scalp by the sudden pink radiance. He shouted in shock and uncertainty.","He looked at the glowing man, then at the little girl standing beside him.","Even a killer who had seen all manner of strange things was left utterly bewildered.","“What kind of demon are you? Stop playing tricks!”","The One-Eyed Dragon quickly regained his composure and swung the long blade in his hand.","“Surround them! Don’t let a single one escape!”","More than a dozen Blood Drip assassins shot into the air, their long blades carving streaks of cold light through the darkness.","In the blink of an eye, Su Yaoyao and Su Jin were surrounded on all sides.","More than a dozen poison-coated blades glimmered with a chilling sheen beneath the moonlight, sealing off every possible escape route.","A suffocating aura of death filled the air.","The One-Eyed Dragon was clearly far more ruthless than the ordinary guards.","He had no intention of taking them alive.","Instead, he walked straight to the warehouse doors.","A gunpowder barrel had apparently been handled carelessly, spilling a scattering of black powder across the ground in front of the doors.","The air reeked of pungent sulfur.","The One-Eyed Dragon gave a cold laugh and pulled a fire striker from inside his robes. With a sharp puff, he lit it.","He held the bright flame above the spilled gunpowder.","“I don’t care whether you’re demons or men. Anyone who causes trouble in Blackwind Stronghold has only one fate—death!”","The One-Eyed Dragon’s eyes were vicious, and his arm trembled as he stood ready to drop the fire striker at any moment.","“Make one wrong move, and we all go to the grave together!”","The flame danced in the cold wind, hovering dangerously close to the gunpowder on the ground.","Su Jin’s pupils contracted sharply. His fingers tightened around his dagger until his knuckles turned white.","The true qi within him surged. He was prepared to force his way through the poison’s effects and kill the One-Eyed Dragon before the fire striker hit the ground, even if it meant fighting to the death.","At that critical moment—","Su Yaoyao calmly let out a sigh.","Then she took a small golden abacus from inside her robes."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: In this life, who would turn their back on money","paragraphs":["Just as Su Jin was about to charge forward at all costs, a small, fair hand firmly pressed against his arm.","Su Yaoyao stepped forward, utterly composed.","She gave the little abacus a crisp flick.","“Click.”","The sharp sound rang out.","The One-Eyed Dragon leader was caught off guard by Su Yaoyao’s sudden move and pulled the firebrand back slightly.","“You little brat. You’re about to die, and you’re still balancing the books?”","The One-Eyed Dragon let out a sinister laugh, convinced that the two of them had been scared witless.","Su Yaoyao raised her head and stared straight at him, her gaze as sharp as a torch.","There was not the slightest trace of fear in her eyes.","“What’s wrong with me balancing the books?”","Su Yaoyao curled her lips, her tone full of disdain.","“You Blood Drippers make your living with your heads tucked into your waistbands.”","“Tell me, how much does that Grand General pay you each month?”","The One-Eyed Dragon was caught completely off guard. His brows drew together into a knot.","What on earth was this little girl thinking?","Was this really the time to discuss salaries?","“What? Are you keeping it confidential?”","Su Yaoyao moved the beads on her abacus, producing a steady clacking sound.","“Let me guess. At most, you get five taels of silver, right?”","“Meals included, lodging not included—and if you’re wounded, you have to pay for your own medicine.”","The flesh on the One-Eyed Dragon’s face twitched.","His heart gave a jolt. How did this girl know their working conditions so well?","The Grand General was indeed cold-blooded. He paid them only that much and had never offered compensation for death.","“What the hell do you know?”","The One-Eyed Dragon gritted his teeth. “We risk our lives for our lord because of a greater cause!”","“A greater cause?”","Su Yaoyao burst out laughing as if she had just heard the funniest joke in the world.","“Can a greater cause put food on the table? Can it buy you a new leg to replace the one that was hacked off at the border?”","“Or is it that after you die, the Grand General will take in your penniless wife and children and support them properly?”","Every question struck directly at the assassins’ deepest vulnerabilities.","The assassins surrounding them, who had been bristling with killing intent, unconsciously lowered their blades.","That was true.","Though they were elite assassins, what kind of lives did they actually lead?","They lived in dark, damp shacks and ate coarse grain and watery vegetables. When they were injured, they could only hide away and nurse themselves back to health.","And if a mission failed, what awaited them was not the Grand General’s protection, but a clean-up operation to silence them.","“Mutually assured destruction?”","A playful curve formed at the corner of Su Yaoyao’s lips. She kicked open the lid of the gunpowder barrel beside her foot.","Looking at the black powder inside, she spoke in a clear, forceful voice.","“Does your lord pay into your social insurance and housing fund?”","“If this place blows up today, which of you will get a pension?”","“If you suffer a serious injury on a mission, will he reimburse your medical expenses?”","The string of unfamiliar terms sounded like an otherworldly language to the assassins.","Yet the sense of security and protection they conveyed burrowed into the assassins’ minds like poison.","“Your current benefits aren’t even as good as those of cargo robots from the interstellar age!”","Seeing that the time was right, Su Yaoyao planted one foot on the edge of the gunpowder barrel.","Her presence surged to its full force, light flashing from her peach-blossom eyes.","“If you’re willing to risk your lives like this, why not find yourselves a proper patron?”","“Join me, the Crown Princess! I’ll triple your base pay!”","“Double pay at year’s end, room and board included, and a complete set of top-quality equipment. All medical expenses covered in full!”","“If one day you happen to die in battle, compensation will be sent directly to your family. They’ll have enough to eat and drink for the rest of their lives!”","“Whatever those corrupt officials are paying you, the Crown Princess will pay three times as much for your lives!”","“You can do the math yourselves, can’t you?”","The square fell utterly silent.","Even the wind seemed to stop.","The assassins gripping their poisoned blades looked at one another, each seeing the hesitation in the others’ eyes.","Compared with this, the treatment offered by the Grand General was nothing but a steaming pile of dog shit.","The conditions offered by this mysterious little girl before them sounded like something only immortals in heaven could enjoy.","They didn’t understand half of it, but it sounded incredibly high-class—and reassuring.","“Boss... ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍you really will cover everything?”","The firebrand in the One-Eyed Dragon’s hand trembled. His killing intent had vanished without a trace, replaced by unconcealed yearning.","“As long as you can fix my leg, this life of mine is yours!”","Su Yaoyao waved her hand grandly, brimming with confidence.","“Not only will I treat you, I’ll also give you the finest iron prosthetic!”","“As long as you lay down your weapons today, all these carts of gunpowder and iron will belong to me!”","“You won’t have to die, and tomorrow you can take your advance pay and go drink and feast!”","“In this life, who would ever turn down money?”","“Choose the wrong employer, and you’re the ones who went blind. Choose the right one, and you’ve found your chance to change your fate!”","The One-Eyed Dragon drew a deep breath.","He looked at the crates of gunpowder and iron gleaming coldly beneath the night sky.","Then he looked at the brothers around him.","Finally, he tossed the firebrand in his hand to the ground.","Clang!","One by one, the long blades slid back into their sheaths.","The One-Eyed Dragon dropped to one knee and spoke in a hoarse but resolute voice.","“To hell with the Grand General! As long as the boss puts food on our tables, we brothers will be the sharpest blades in her hand!”","“Long live the boss!”","Dozens of assassins knelt in perfect unison, their voices shaking the heavens.","Su Yaoyao put away her abacus, a sly smile flashing through her eyes.","She looked at this group of elite special forces, then at the iron and gunpowder.","This haul had made her rich beyond belief!","“Hehe, the iron and gunpowder are all mine now.”","Su Yaoyao turned around and looked at the underlings helping pack up the supplies.","The corners of her mouth lifted into a dangerous, icy smile.","“Grand General, you went to such great lengths to build up this stockpile, but the Crown Princess will be taking every last bit of it.”","“At the Mid-Autumn banquet, I’ll prepare an extra-special Gatling-gun surprise for you.”","“I hope your psychological resilience won’t disappoint me when the time comes.”","The firelight at Black Wind Stronghold gradually died out.","More than a dozen large carriages slowly departed into the night, carrying the reformed assassin squad and ten full carts of military-grade materials toward the depths of the imperial palace.","With a black sack over his head, Su Jin occasionally hopped a few steps in an awkward yet strangely smooth moonwalk.","After listening to his sister’s ambitious thoughts, he still felt they were absurd—but an unexpected sense of anticipation had begun to stir in his heart.","This was far more interesting than those games from before.","His little sister was truly the kind of person who could tear a hole straight through the sky.","And he, it seemed, was stepping onto a path he had never once imagined.","The moon gradually faded from view.","The triumphant convoy disappeared into the thick night.","Su Yaoyao sat at the front of the carriage, idly twirling the lid of a gunpowder barrel in her hand.","She calculated the materials she now possessed, then glanced toward the imperial palace."]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: Your Highness, how can you still be thinking about money at a time like this","paragraphs":["Inside Zhaoyang Hall, sunlight streamed through the carved window lattices and spilled across the golden-thread nanmu desk.","Su Yaoyao was sprawled over the desk, clutching a charred willow twig that she used as a charcoal pencil.","On the finest xuan paper, she was scribbling and sketching a complicated blueprint that no one in this era could possibly understand.","“The Gatling gun’s rotating barrel mechanism needs more optimization.”","“The Great Abyss Kingdom’s smelting technology is far too backward. To meet the barrel’s requirements for high strength and heat resistance, I’ll have to add Black Ice Stone.”","“The gunpowder purification ratio needs to be adjusted too, or the barrel could easily explode.”","Su Yaoyao gnawed on the end of her charcoal stick as she rapidly calculated every figure on the paper.","But the more she calculated, the more her delicate, doll-like face fell.","She was out of money!","Although she had just received a commission of seventy-five thousand taels from the property confiscated from the Left Censor’s family by her Tyrant Dad,","and although the basic materials she had acquired during her free raid on Blackwind Stronghold had helped ease the immediate crisis,","this was a project to manufacture heavy-firepower weapons!","Seventy-five thousand taels might sound like a great deal, but if she really wanted to set up an entire production line, it would not even be enough to fill a tooth!","Not to mention that just placing bounties on rare ores and components through the black market would cost a fortune.","No, she had to find a way to raise more funding.","Su Yaoyao stroked her chubby little chin, the abacus in her mind clacking away.","Just as she was racking her brains and calculating which corrupt official in the capital she could visit next—","“Your Highness! Your Highness!”","Her personal maid, Cui’er, came hurrying into the hall, her face brimming with indignation.","“What is it? Don’t tell me someone has come to give me money again?”","Su Yaoyao’s eyes lit up as she tossed aside her charcoal stick.","“Your Highness, how can you still be thinking about money at a time like this?” Cui’er stamped her feet anxiously. “Someone from the Grand General’s residence has entered the palace!”","The Grand General, Lin Zhenxiong?","Su Yaoyao raised an eyebrow.","Only last night, she had taken her bargain-bin older brother to empty the armory in the Grand General’s outer compound.","And today, the old man had already sent someone into the palace?","He certainly moved fast.","“The person who entered the palace is the Grand General’s distant grandniece. Her name is Lin Wan’er,” Cui’er hurriedly reported. “I hear Miss Lin is known as the capital’s foremost talented lady. She’s accomplished in music, chess, calligraphy, and painting.”","“The Grand General deliberately sent her into the palace to study alongside you. He’s clearly trying to give you a warning!”","After hearing this, Su Yaoyao did not get angry. Instead, she laughed, the corners of her mouth curving into an amused smile.","“Oh? The capital’s foremost talented lady?”","“Where is she now?”","“She’s in the Imperial Garden!” Cui’er bit her lip, looking deeply indignant.","“Miss Lin has set up some sort of Chrysanthemum Appreciation Charity Banquet and invited all the empresses, consorts, and noble ladies in the palace.”","“She claims it’s to raise money for winter clothing for the soldiers guarding the frontier, but isn’t she just insulting you in a roundabout way?”","The moment Su Yaoyao heard the words “charity banquet,” her radar started blaring.","A charity banquet? Isn’t that just an ancient version of a fundraiser?","A group of wealthy ladies and noblewomen gathered together, competing to show off their riches while scattering silver by the handful.","It was a massive fresh-leek harvesting operation—and it was about to begin!","Su Yaoyao immediately perked up. Just moments ago, she had been worrying about how to fund her military research and development.","And now, the Grand General had not only delivered gunpowder to her doorstep, but had even sent a relative to deliver her research funds!","What a wonderful man!","“Come on, Cui’er. Let’s go take a stroll around the Imperial Garden.”","Su Yaoyao hopped down from her chair and dusted the charcoal ash from her hands.","“If we’re late, the big fat sheep might get plucked bald by someone else!”","The Imperial Garden was in full bloom, with a subtle fragrance drifting through the air.","Inside a pavilion, consorts from the various palaces and noble ladies from the capital sat in a circle, chatting and laughing.","Seated at the very center of them all was none other than Lin Wan’er, the capital’s foremost talented lady.","Lin Wan’er wore a plain, elegant moon-white gauze dress. The only ornament in her hair was a simple silver hairpin.","She looked pure and otherworldly, as delicate as a willow in the wind—as though the slightest breeze might blow her away.","Among the extravagantly dressed women of the inner palace, her appearance seemed especially pitiful and distinctive.","“Miss Lin, your poem praising the chrysanthemums is truly refined and exceptional. It’s enough to make anyone slap the table in admiration.”","A consort who usually depended on the Grand General’s influence held a silk handkerchief and showered her with praise.","“That’s ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍right, that’s right. She truly is worthy of being the capital’s foremost talented lady.”","“Compared with certain uncouth people who were just brought back from the black market, they’re worlds apart.”","“If you ask me, only a well-bred young lady like Miss Lin—one who is knowledgeable and sensible—is worthy of the dignity of the imperial palace.”","The noblewomen chimed in one after another, every word carrying a veiled jab at Su Yaoyao.","As Lin Wan’er listened to their flattery, a flash of triumph crossed her eyes.","On the surface, however, she put on a frightened and helpless expression.","“Ladies, please don’t say such things. Although Your Highness spent years wandering among the common people and never had the opportunity to study the sages’ classics...”","“She is still His Majesty’s bloodline. We ought to be more understanding.”","Lin Wan’er lightly dabbed at the corners of her eyes with her handkerchief and sighed.","“I did not arrange today’s banquet to compete in talent. I was merely thinking that autumn winds are beginning to blow, while the soldiers at the frontier are still suffering in the cold.”","“The Grand General often says that the rise and fall of the nation is everyone’s responsibility.”","“Although I am only a woman, I still wish to contribute in whatever small way I can. That is why I took the liberty of inviting all my sisters here, so that together we might raise some funds to provide the soldiers with winter clothing.”","Her words were so righteous and compassionate that they immediately drew a wave of praise from the surrounding women, who began generously opening their purses.","“I’ll donate fifty taels!”","“I’ll contribute a pair of Hotan jade bracelets!”","Lin Wan’er smiled as she had her maid record each donation. Then, as if unintentionally, she let out another sigh.","“I only regret that I’ve heard Your Highness has amassed a tremendous fortune through the black market, yet is notoriously stingy.”","“If Your Highness were willing to contribute even the tiniest portion of that ill-gotten wealth, the soldiers at the frontier would no longer have to worry about surviving the winter.”","“Alas, I fear that in Your Highness’s eyes, there is only money. She probably doesn’t understand what national duty means.”","The moment these words were spoken, everyone’s disdain for the Imperial Crown Princess grew even stronger.","Just as they were preparing to continue condemning the Imperial Crown Princess as a miser, a crisp, teasing voice drifted in from outside the pavilion.","“Well, well, what’s all the excitement about?”","“I could smell the strong scent of green tea from a mile away. So it turns out my cousin is brewing tea here?”","Everyone turned toward the voice in unison.","They saw Su Yaoyao approaching in a fiery-red brocade vest, both hands clasped behind her back as she swaggered toward them.","Her large, black eyes, round as grapes, were filled with mocking amusement.","Tsk, tsk, tsk. Today I’ve actually encountered a genuine, top-tier green-tea schemer.","Her talent for speaking in fake-sweet, self-righteous platitudes is only enough to fool this bunch of embittered women from the inner palace.","On the surface, this is a fundraiser for winter clothing. In reality, isn’t she helping the Grand General launder money while building her own reputation and stepping on me in the process?","You want to use my head as a stepping stone to rise higher? Fine. Today, this Crown Princess will teach you exactly what a weed whacker can do!","When Lin Wan’er saw Su Yaoyao appear, she froze.","Soon, an expression of panic and grievance surfaced on her delicate face.","Like a startled little rabbit, she hurriedly rose from the stone stool.","“Your Highness... Lin Wan’er pays her respects to Your Highness.”","Lin Wan’er bent gracefully at the waist, her body appearing fragile and delicate.","“Just now, I was merely chatting with the ladies. I absolutely did not mean to speak ill of Your Highness behind your back.”","“If Your Highness heard anything unpleasant, Wan’er apologizes on their behalf. Please, Your Highness, don’t be angry.”","She looked pitiful enough to seem as though she had already been bullied, even though no one had touched her.","The sight immediately stirred the protective instincts of the women around them.","Several of the bolder consorts stepped forward and shielded Lin Wan’er behind them.","“Your Highness, Miss Lin kindly organized this charity drive for everyone. Not only are you refusing to help, but you’ve come here to throw your weight around?”","“You’ve been running wild in the black market for so long. Don’t tell me you intend to cause a scene here in the Imperial Garden?”","Watching this group of indignant noblewomen, Su Yaoyao couldn’t even be bothered to roll her eyes. She walked straight to the stone table, picked up a delicate osmanthus cake, and stuffed it into her mouth.","“Relax. It’s not like I’m here to eat people.”","Su Yaoyao mumbled around the pastry as she chewed.","“I heard from Cui’er that my cousin was hosting a charity banquet here, so I came over to see if there was anything fun going on.”","Lin Wan’er hadn’t expected Su Yaoyao not to play along. Instead of flying into a rage and arguing with them, she had simply ignored their insults.","Lin Wan’er couldn’t help letting out a cold laugh inwardly.","As expected, she really was a brainless fool. She couldn’t even tell when people were insulting her.","Since you’ve delivered yourself into my hands, don’t blame me for humiliating you in front of everyone!","Lin Wan’er took a deep breath, then put her holy, aggrieved smile back on her face.","“We’re truly honored that Your Highness could come.”","“Since Your Highness has also come for the soldiers stationed at the frontier, I assume you’ve brought a generous donation as well?”","Lin Wan’er deliberately raised her voice so that everyone could hear her clearly.","“Wan’er knows that Your Highness has operated in the black market for many years and must have an impressive fortune—certainly beyond what weak women like us could ever compare with.”","“However, relying solely on gold and silver does seem rather vulgar.”","Her tone shifted, and a proud look appeared between her brows.","“For this charity drive, I specially asked my father to purchase a peerless mechanical treasure from a neighboring kingdom at great expense.”","“Wan’er intends to display it before everyone and auction it off to raise funds.”","“If Your Highness could also produce a suitably elegant treasure, the two of us sisters could offer our prayers for the soldiers together. Wouldn’t that make a beautiful story?”","The noblewomen around them immediately began whispering among themselves.","“Miss Lin is challenging Your Highness to a contest of family wealth!”","“That country girl knows nothing except gold and silver. How could she understand mechanical treasures or anything truly refined?”","“This time, the Crown Princess is going to make a fool of herself!”","Listening to the surrounding gossip, the little flame in Su Yaoyao’s heart didn’t die down. Instead, it burned even more fiercely.","[Oh, please. You want to compete with me in mechanics? In high technology?]","[I’m the finest engineer in the entire interstellar era! Even the parts I can cobble together with my eyes closed would be superior to your national treasure!]","[Fine. I’d love to see what pile of scrap metal the Grand General’s residence can produce.]","Su Yaoyao dusted the crumbs from her hands and raised her brows with keen interest.","“Sure. Bring it out and let me broaden my horizons.”","Seeing that the fish had taken the bait, Lin Wan’er was ecstatic.","She turned gracefully and gave a slight nod to the maidservant standing behind her.","The maid respectfully presented an exquisite rosewood box.","“This object was crafted by a master artisan from a neighboring kingdom after ten years of painstaking work. It is called the Ruyi Musical Box.”","Lin Wan’er’s voice was brimming with undisguised pride.","Under the expectant gazes of all the women present, she reached out and slowly opened the rosewood box.","“Wow!”","The moment the box opened, the consorts and noblewomen surrounding them let out a collective gasp.","One by one, they craned their necks forward, their eyes filled with amazement and admiration.","“How exquisite! It’s practically the work of Heaven itself!”","“Such a rare treasure—I’ve never heard of or seen anything like it!”","Amid the exaggerated praise, Su Yaoyao also rose onto her toes and stretched her neck to take a look.","But the moment she got a clear view of the peerless treasure inside the box, the curiosity on her face froze.","Her peach blossom eyes widened as she stared at the object within.","A powerful urge to burst into laughter shot straight to her head.","She clenched her back teeth so hard that she barely managed not to let out a sound like a squealing pig right there on the spot.","They actually dared to show off this thing?"]}]);
